EXAM_DATA['cis-df'] = {"exam":{"code":"CIS-DF","title":"ServiceNow CIS-DF Flashcards","subtitle":"Certified Implementation Specialist – Data Foundations (CMDB & CSDM)"},"contexts":[],"questions":[{"n":1,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator has built a number of Technology Management Service Offerings (Technical Service Offerings) based on Dynamic CI Groups to better maintain group alignment for the member CI.\n\nWhich Groups are synced to CIs from the offering that has a relationship to a Dynamic CI Group? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Approval Group","B":"Managed by Group","C":"Support Group","D":"Owned by Group"},"answer":"BC"},{"n":2,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROP\n\nDrag and drop the application service type to the best description.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image2.png\">"},{"n":3,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A new custom class is needed to reflect a new application being managed in the CMDB.\n\nWhich roles are minimally needed to add this custom CI class?","choices":{"A":"A cmdb_inst_admin and personalize_form","B":"itil_admin and personalize_form","C":"data_classification_admin and personalize_dictionary","D":"sn_cmdb_admin and personalize_dictionary Most Voted"},"answer":"D"},{"n":4,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"What is the relationship between an application and a server?","choices":{"A":"Application>Used by::Uses>Server","B":"Application> Uses::Used by>Server","C":"Application>Runs::Runs On>Server","D":"Application>Runs on::Runs>Server Most Voted"},"answer":"D"},{"n":5,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"User endpoint devices are imported into the CMDB and populate the ‘Assigned to’ [assigned_to] field on the Computer [cmdb_ci_computer] CI. The Asset team puts in a request for the Configuration Analysts to populate the ‘Assigned to’ field on the related Asset.\n\nWhat action does a Configuration Analyst take to achieve this in an automated way?","choices":{"A":"Use the Asset-CI Field Mapping module to create a new rule to replicate the ‘Assigned to’ value between the asset and associated CI Most Voted","B":"Hide the ‘Assigned to’ field on the asset record and create a new field that dot walks to the related CI to get the ‘Assigned to’ value","C":"Configure a business rule on the computer table to use a script to populate the ‘Assigned to’ filed on the asset based on insert or update in the computer class ‘Assigned to’ field"},"answer":"A"},{"n":6,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator needs to create a new CI class for the Internet of Things (IoT) Sensor in ServiceNow.\n\nWhat are the recommended practices for this specific activity? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Add a new class under an appropriate parent class","B":"Modify an existing class","C":"Install or update the CMDB CI Class Models store application, and verify the class does not already exist","D":"Delete an unused class, and replace it with the new one"},"answer":"AC"},{"n":7,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A Change Manager aims to streamline ITSM processes by automatically populating fields on the Change form when a CI is selected. The Configuration Management team is working to ensure that the Change Group field is populated for all managed CIs.\n\nAs a result, which base system field on the incident form will be automatically populated after selecting a CI?","choices":{"A":"Managed by group","B":"Approval group","C":"Assignment group","D":"Change group"},"answer":"C"},{"n":8,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A Data Center Manager is working with the CMDB CI Class Manager to define the relationship between Application Servers and the Applications they host. The company has multiple Application Servers that host one or more Applications.\n\nWhich describes the relationship between the Application Server table ([cmdb_ci_app_server]) and the Application table ([cmdb_ci_appl])?","choices":{"A":"Many-to-one","B":"One-to-one","C":"One-to-many","D":"Many-to-many Most Voted"},"answer":"D"},{"n":9,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator needs to identify which attributes have been created specifically for the Windows Server class.\n\nWhich tab in the Attributes section is used?","choices":{"A":"All","B":"Derived","C":"Added","D":"Child"},"answer":"C"},{"n":10,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"An Asset Manager wants to ensure that Asset records and CI records are kept synchronized automatically.\n\nHow does the Manager do this? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Ensure one-to-one physical mapping between Asset and CI","B":"Ensure that scheduled jobs are run during off-business hours to ensure sync happens","C":"Ensure that the business rule to update Asset fields on change on the CI table is active","D":"Ensure that the business rule to update CI fields on change on the asset table is active"},"answer":"CD"},{"n":11,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"The CMDB Configuration Management team has successfully developed a healthy and trusted CMDB. They have integrated discovered infrastructure data, accurately referenced non-discoverable data (such as change and support group information), and made the CMDB service-aware using Service Mapping.\n\nWhich field on an Incident form is automatically populated after a CI is selected that references an appropriate support group?","choices":{"A":"Support Group","B":"Approval Group","C":"Change Group","D":"Assignment Group","E":"Managed by Group"},"answer":"D"},{"n":12,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Management Process Owner is preparing solution options for presentation to the technical governance board for ingesting custom CIs to the CMDB. The solution needs to align with best practice, minimize the cost of future work (technical debt) and ensure compliance with future upgrades.\n\nWhich solutions accomplish this? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Repurposing a base CI class and rename attributes, as required","B":"Extending an existing CI class table to accommodate the custom CI class attributes","C":"Installing or upgrading the ‘CMDB CI Class Models’ store application to find a suitable existing CI class accommodating any new attributes","D":"Extending an existing Asset class table to accommodate the custom CI class attributes"},"answer":"BC"},{"n":13,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants only the CIs of Principal Classes to appear in CI reference fields, for example the CI reference fields accessible from an Incident Form.\n\nWhere does the CMDB Administrator designate Principal Classes?","choices":{"A":"CI Class Manager Most Voted","B":"CMDB Workspace","C":"CMDB Data Manager","D":"System Properties"},"answer":"A"},{"n":14,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager is managing a CI class in the CMDB. The identification rule(s) needs an update.\n\nWhere can the Configuration Manager view and configure the existing identification rule(s) for the class? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"CI Identifiers module","B":"API Integrations","C":"IRE Application","D":"CI Class Manager Most Voted"},"answer":"AD"},{"n":15,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to ensure that only relevant CIs from managed classes will be shown on Incident, Problem, and Change records.\n\nWhich checkbox needs to be checked in the CI Class Manager for the CMDB Administrator to achieve the requested result?","choices":{"A":"Principal Class Most Voted","B":"Independent","C":"Main Record","D":"Extensible"},"answer":"A"},{"n":16,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Management team has decided to start taking advantage of the CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB functionality.\n\nWhich system property must be enabled?","choices":{"A":"glide.identification_engine.multisource_enabled Most Voted","B":"glide.identification_engine.multisource.query.max.limit","C":"glide.identification_engine.multisource_non_cmdb_ci_enabled","D":"glide.identification_engine.multisource_cmdb_ci_enabled"},"answer":"A"},{"n":17,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is creating technical documentation for stakeholders, which includes a list of attributes, Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE) rules, and suggested relationships for several classes.\n\nWhich central location does the CMDB Administrator use to collect this information?","choices":{"A":"CI Class Manager Most Voted","B":"CI Identifiers","C":"CMDB Workspace","D":"CMDB Data Manager"},"answer":"A"},{"n":18,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to configure IRE rules for the CMDB. The CMDB Administrator opens CI Class Manager and sees the Health Inclusions Rules tab available under a CI Class.\n\nHow are these rules utilized by the IRE?","choices":{"A":"To narrow the scope of CIs included in the identification process","B":"To reduce the data ingested into the CMDB","C":"To reconcile specific attributes based on data sources"},"answer":"A"},{"n":19,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A Windows administration team wants a grouping of CIs using CMDB groups.\n\nWhich methods can be used? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Tag-based queries","B":"Scripted queries","C":"Saved queries","D":"Encoded queries"},"answer":"CD"},{"n":20,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is managing group data from both the CI Class Manager and a Technical Service Offering for a specific class.\n\nCl Class Manager:\n\n- Managed by Group = Enterprise IT Services\n\nTechnical Service Offering:\n\n- Managed by Group = Windows Support\n\n- Change Group = Change Management Team\n\nWhat would be the Managed By Group for CIs from this class based on the configured values?","choices":{"A":"Windows Support Most Voted","B":"Enterprise IT Services","C":"Change Management Team"},"answer":"A"},{"n":21,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager wants to manage manually maintained data attributes of CIs. Which group values are automatically synchronized on CIs using Technology Management Offerings (Technical Service Offerings) and dynamic CI groups? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Change group","B":"Approval group","C":"Support group","D":"CMDB group"},"answer":"AC"},{"n":22,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is tasked with managing the CMDB and needs to define a new CI class to track a new type of equipment that has not been seen before. Which action adds a new CI class and ensures it integrates properly with the existing CMDB structure?","choices":{"A":"Use Service Catalog to define the new CI class, as the CI Class Manager is only for service-related records and not for hardware CIs","B":"Edit an existing CI class under CI Class Manager and add new fields specific to the new equipment type","C":"Create a new CI class directly in the CI Class Manager and configure the table inheritance to ensure it inherits from a relevant parent class","D":"Use the CI Class Manager to create a new CI class but avoid setting up any inheritance, as CI classes should be independent of one another to maintain clarity"},"answer":"C"},{"n":23,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager needs to restrict the number of classes available in a Configuration Item reference field on an incident form. How does the Manager set Principal Classes?","choices":{"A":"By using the Principal Class check box on the CI Class Manager's 'Basic Info' tab for a Class Most Voted","B":"By using the Principal Class check box on the CI Class Manager's 'Attributes' tab for a Class","C":"By using the Principal Class attribute on the CI","D":"By using the Principal Class check box on the CMDB Workspace"},"answer":"A"},{"n":24,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator aims to utilize CSDM life cycle field mappings to better align with CSDM best practices. What is the next step to take after selecting the Enable Life Cycle Sync button?","choices":{"A":"Resolve any incomplete field mappings identified in the Discrepancy Report","B":"Fix the incorrect values in the Life Cycle Stage to match legacy values","C":"Activate the CSDM Life Cycle field mappings"},"answer":"A"},{"n":25,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator needs to set a CI Class as a Principal Class. Which CI Class Manager tab would need to be accessed?","choices":{"A":"Health > Attributes","B":"Class Info > Attributes","C":"Class Info > Basic Info"},"answer":"C"},{"n":26,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A ServiceNow Administrator needs to create multiple new classes in the CMDB but wants to follow ServiceNow's best practices for naming CMDB tables to prevent technical debt. Which is the starting prefix for all custom CMDB tables?","choices":{"A":"ci_cmdb","B":"cmdb_ci","C":"u_cmdb_ci Most Voted","D":"u_ci_cmdb"},"answer":"C"},{"n":27,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Management team needs to prevent duplicate server records to avoid confusion among users. Server records are identified when they are processed via the Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE) using the configured identification rules. Where would these rules be configured?","choices":{"A":"CMDB Workspace","B":"CMDB CI Class Manager","C":"CMDB Health Dashboard","D":"CMDB Data Manager"},"answer":"B"},{"n":28,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator notices that CIs do not have a support group. How can the support group be automatically populated and maintained on the CI record?","choices":{"A":"Technology Management Service Offering (Technical Service Offering) Most Voted","B":"Technology Management Service (Technical Service)","C":"CI Class Manager","D":"Dynamic CI group"},"answer":"A"},{"n":29,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"Using CI Class Manager, the Tomcat identification rule has the following criterion attributes configured: • Class • Install Directory Which identifier entry configuration option must be checked to attempt a match using the Application identification rule if no match is found using the Tomcat identification rule?","choices":{"A":"Allow fallback to parent's rules","B":"Independent","C":"Applies to","D":"Criterion attributes"},"answer":"A"},{"n":30,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB CI Class Owner has been asked to change the icon for the UNIX Server class. Which CI Class Manager tab can the owner use to change the icon for the class?","choices":{"A":"CI List","B":"Basic Info","C":"Attributes","D":"Suggested Relationships"},"answer":"B"},{"n":31,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager is reviewing the life cycle of CIs to e nsure data accuracy, consistency, and relevance. The manager reviews the legacy status values and the ir equivalent CSDM life cycle stage and life cycle stage status values. Where are these reviewed?","choices":{"A":"Life cycle choice list","B":"Life cycle mappings","C":"Life cycle properties"},"answer":"B"},{"n":32,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"An organization is updating the CMDB to include new asset types like IoT devices. Relevant CI classes need to be added and outdated ones need to be removed from the Principal Class filter to ensure accurate display in ITSM processes.Which roles are needed to add or remove classes? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"personalize_dictionary","B":"sn_csdm_admin","C":"sn_cmdb_admin","D":"cmdb_query_builder"},"answer":"AC"},{"n":33,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"An IT group has a requirement to upgrade all the Windows server s. There is a Dynamic CI Group containing all the Windows servers. What happens to the Dynamic CI Group when it is referenced from the Configuration Item field on a Change form?","choices":{"A":"It displays all related CIs in the Impacted Services related list.","B":"It calculates impact against the Dynamic CI Group.","C":"It displays all related CIs in the Affected CIs related list."},"answer":"C"},{"n":34,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is working in the CI Class Manager on the Basic Info tab. How can the class be set as a Principal Class?","choices":{"A":"Check the Principal Class check box","B":"Click the Principal Class UI Action button","C":"Select 'Yes' from the Principal Class choice list"},"answer":"A"},{"n":35,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A global enterprise integrates data from multiple discovery sou rces such as ServiceNow Discovery, SCCM, AWS, and manual uploads to populate its CMDB. However, ea ch discovery source categorizes the same CIs differently, leading to duplicate records and inconsis tencies across the system. As a result, the CMDB team is struggling with data accuracy and standardization. What actions does the CMDB team take to resolve the issue? (Cho ose two.)","choices":{"A":"Allow each discovery source to define its own CI class, even if it results in inconsistencies","B":"Implement and use identification and reconciliation rules to avoid duplicates and standardize CI classification","C":"Create a custom script to manually adjust incoming data befor e storing it in the CMDB","D":"Use CI Class Manager to establish standardized CI classes and attributes across all discovery sources"},"answer":"BD"},{"n":36,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB CI Class Owner responsible for the Windows Servers needs to manage the Windows Server class. Which CI Class Manager feature will help the CI Class Owner str eamline this task?","choices":{"A":"Pinned Classes","B":"CI Favorites","C":"Search CI Classes"},"answer":"A"},{"n":37,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"The Change Management team in an organization wants to implemen t a Change across multiple CIs at the same time. Which field on the Change Request form needs to be populated wi th a dynamic CI group?","choices":{"A":"Configuration Item","B":"Business Service","C":"Service Offering"},"answer":"A"},{"n":38,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator needs to configure a new application ident ification rule that considers the potential for the same application installed more than once on the same s erver. Which is the best choice of a criterion attribute?","choices":{"A":"Version","B":"Configuration File Name","C":"Port","D":"Configuration File Path","E":"Class"},"answer":"D"},{"n":39,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROP A CMDB Administrator needs to set up CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB. Drag and drop the system property to the functionality. Some options may not apply.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image35.png\">"},{"n":40,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Manager is in the crawl stage of their CMDB journey and would like to follow the Common Service Data Model. What domains would be addressed? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Manage Technical Services","B":"Foundation","C":"Design","D":"Sell/Consume"},"answer":"A"},{"n":44,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to add a reconciliation rule using CI Class Manager. However, the Administrator is not given the choice to select between Static and Dynamic. How are these options made available?","choices":{"A":"Elevate the role to ‘security_admin’","B":"Modify the system property ‘glide.dynamic_reconciliation.allowed_classes’","C":"Activate the system property ‘glide.identification_engine.multisource_enabled’","D":"Navigate to the ‘Reconciliation Rules’ module, and enable the ‘Dynamic Rules’ option"},"answer":"C"},{"n":46,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"What functionality is offered on a CI record in the CMDB to easily relate CIs together?","choices":{"A":"Suggested Relationships","B":"Relationship Editor","C":"Unified Map","D":"CI Class Manager"},"answer":"B"},{"n":47,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"The CMDB Administrator has set-up two Dynamic Reconcilliation Rules within the ServiceNow Production Instance. The ‘Server’ class has a Dynamic Reconciliation Rule of largest value for the RAM field. The ‘Windows Server’ class has a Dynamic Reconciliation Rule of most reported for the RAM field.Given the above data in the Multisource CMDB, which value would be added to the CMDB for RAM for a ‘Server’ CI?","choices":{"A":"4.096 MB","B":"8.192 MB","C":"2.048 MB"},"answer":"B"},{"n":48,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator needs to import external data into the CMDB. As the CMDB Administrator wants to reduce the risk for creating duplicates and to update information from unauthorized sources, it has to be ensured that the Identification and Reconciliation API will not be bypassed.What is the recommended method to import data into the CMDB utilizing the Identification and Reconciliation API?","choices":{"A":"IntegrationHub ETL","B":"Table API (REST API or SOAP API)","C":"Import Sets and Transform Maps"},"answer":"A"},{"n":49,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager has configured a multiple data sources which are all authorized to update the same class and the same set of class attributes in the CMDB.What can the Configuration Manager do to control which data source should be authoritative source of truth for a specific class of set of class attributes?","choices":{"A":"Assign a priority to each data source in the reconciliation rules","B":"Manually run the data source updates in the correct order","C":"Configure data refresh rules with a specific time period","D":"Assign a run order to each data source in the identification rules"},"answer":"A"},{"n":50,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"Which CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB the Dynamic Reconciliation Rules will also be enabled. Based on the request of the management, a CMDB Administrator has to set up multiple Dynamic Reconciliation Rules.Which are available ‘Dynamic Rule Types’ within the ‘Create Reconciliation Rule’ wizard? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Last Updated","B":"Smallest Value","C":"Last Created","D":"Most Reported"},"answer":"BD"},{"n":51,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"The following identification rule for a CI class has been defined:Two new CI records are imported into the hardware class of the CMDB:CI1: The name of this CI record matches the name of an existing CI record in the CMDB.CI2: The IP address of this CI record matches the IP address of an existing CI record in the CMDB.Which is correct based on the identification rule and the imported CI records?","choices":{"A":"CI1 will be inserted as new record and CI2 will be updated with matching record.","B":"CI1 will be updated with matching record and CI2 will be inserted as new record.","C":"CI1 and CI2 both will be updated with matching records.","D":"CI1 and CI2 both will be inserted as new records."},"answer":"B"},{"n":52,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"A customer wants recently imported server records to be automatically reclassified into more specific CMDB classes after being discovered using ServiceNow Discovery.During the discovery process, if existing Server [cmdb_ci_server] records are reclassified into the Linux [cmdb_ci_linux_server] and Windows Server [cmdb_ci_win_server] classes, which reclassification operation occurred?","choices":{"A":"Class Upgrade","B":"Class Downgrade","C":"Class Switch"},"answer":"A"},{"n":53,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A Platform Data Owner wants to improve data quality with a few reconciliation rules across the five discovery sources that are being used. The Data Owner knows the best option is to include CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB to manage and monitor discovery sources, but the company currently does not have a license for ITOM Discovery that is required for CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB.What can the Data Owner do in this case?","choices":{"A":"ITOM Discovery needs to be purchased to take advantage of the multisource IRE Rules.","B":"CMBD 360/Multisource is a platform product that can be used immediately.","C":"The IRE reconciliation rules can use discovery source regardless of CMDB 360 being enabled."},"answer":"C"},{"n":54,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"Which ServiceNow solution creates automatic relationships?","choices":{"A":"IntegrationHub ETL","B":"Discovery","C":"Workflow Studio","D":"Service Mapping"},"answer":"B"},{"n":55,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"The Apache Web Server Identification Rule is configured with the following Criterion attributes:Class -Configuration file -Version -Yesterday, an Apache Web Server CI was discovered as part of Service Mapping. Today, the application owner upgraded Apache to a different version and reran discovery of the service.What will happen in the CMDB?","choices":{"A":"The existing Apache Web Server CI will be reconciled and its version will be updated.","B":"A duplication error will occur.","C":"The Apache Web Server CI will be reclassified as a Web Server CI.","D":"A new Apache Web Server CI is created."},"answer":"D"},{"n":56,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"Configuration Management requires an accurate inventory of devi ces to be reflected in the CMDB. Which are common use cases for using Agent Client Collector (AC C)? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Network devices in the DMZ","B":"Devices that intermittently connect to the network","C":"Servers in the data center","D":"Devices in secure environments"},"answer":"BD"},{"n":57,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"An organization needs to maintain non-discoverable attributes, such as warranty expiration dates, for hardware CIs. These attributes are not updated by automated discovery tools.What method ensures these attributes are accurately maintained for all CIs?","choices":{"A":"Create a new CI class specifically for non-discoverable attributes","B":"Use the CMDB Reconciliation Engine to update the attributes","C":"Use a scheduled data import to update the attributes from an external source"},"answer":"C"},{"n":58,"domain":"Data Sources & Ingestion","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROPServiceNow provides a suite of CMDB management tools designed to effectively ingest, manage, and maintain CIs and relationships.Drag and drop the design architecture to its management tool.Some options may not apply.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image7.png\">"},{"n":59,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"When integrating data into the CMDB using import sets and transform maps, which type of script is added to ensure the data is processed through the IRE?","choices":{"A":"onBefore","B":"onComplete","C":"onStart","D":"onAfter"},"answer":"A"},{"n":60,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"The following Reconciliation Rules were configured for ServiceNow, Altiris, and SCCM:Which are true? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Data collected with a discovery source of SCCM can update any record in the Windows Server [cmdb_ci_win_server] table because it has the highest priority number.","B":"Data collected with a discovery source of ServiceNow can insert new records into the Windows Server [cmdb_ci_win_server] table, but cannot update records created by Altiris or SCCM.","C":"Data collected with a discovery source of Altiris can update records inserted by SCCM into the Windows Server [cmdb_ci_win_server] table.","D":"Data collected with a discovery source of SCCM can be inserted as new records in the Windows Server [cmdb_ci_win_server] table."},"answer":"CD"},{"n":61,"domain":"Service Graph Connectors","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator has installed a Service Graph Connector and customized a script transform.What will happen on subsequent upgrades if the default definition of the script transform is updated?","choices":{"A":"A skipped change is created and no change is made the script transform definition.","B":"The Service Graph Connector upgrade refuses to start.","C":"The upgrade stops and reports an error."},"answer":"A"},{"n":62,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A Windows server is reclassified from the Server table [cmdb_ci _server] to the Windows Server table [cmdb_ci_win_server] when processed through the Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE). Which process occurred?","choices":{"A":"Class Change","B":"Class Switch","C":"Class Downgrade","D":"Class Upgrade"},"answer":"D"},{"n":63,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROP\n\nDrag and drop the product to its description.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image21.png\"><img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image22.png\">"},{"n":64,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"An organization utilizes multiple data sources to update its CM DB, each assigned a different priority level. A high-priority data source is scheduled to update server recor ds weekly. However, due to an integration issue, the high-priority data source stops updating the records . Which configuration can be used to allow a lower-priority data source to update records after a specified period of inactivity from the higher-priority source?","choices":{"A":"Data Refresh Rules","B":"Reconciliation Rules","C":"Health Inclusion Rules","D":"Identification Rules"},"answer":"A"},{"n":65,"domain":"Service Graph Connectors","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator has imported data into the ServiceNow CMDB from a third-party source using a Service Graph Connector. The Administrator wants to review spec ific field to field mappings for the import. Which feature will show that information?","choices":{"A":"Integration Hub","B":"IntegrationHub ETL","C":"CMDB Integrations Dashboard"},"answer":"B"},{"n":66,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"What are the characteristics or functions of ServiceNow Integra tionHub ETL? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Integrates third-party data into the CMDB or into non-CM DB tables","B":"Uses the IRE to process and integrate data","C":"Imports Microsoft SCCM/Intune data into the CMDB","D":"Performs discovery data collection and updates the CMDB"},"answer":"AB"},{"n":67,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator needs to ingest relevant data from Microso ft SCCM into the CMDB. Which ingestion method brings the fastest time to value?","choices":{"A":"Import Sets","B":"Service Graph Connectors","C":"Agent Client Collector","D":"IntegrationHub ETL"},"answer":"B"},{"n":68,"domain":"Service Graph Connectors","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator changes the query for the SCCM Service Gra ph Connector. What is the impact of this change?","choices":{"A":"Any Scheduled Jobs for the SCCM Service Graph Connector will need to be configured.","B":"Any updates for the SCCM Service Graph Connector will be skip ped during the upgrade.","C":"The Data Source for the SCCM Service Graph Connector will be marked as Inactive."},"answer":"B"},{"n":69,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator needs to prevent duplicate CI creation from import sets that load data into the CMDB from vendor shipment files containing CI information.How can the Administrator do this?","choices":{"A":"Set the coalesce on two mappings within the transform map","B":"Create comparison rules in the IRE","C":"Set the system property to utilize the IRE within transform maps","D":"Use the CMDBTransformUtil API in the transform script"},"answer":"D"},{"n":70,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A ServiceNow Administrator wants to implement Service Graph Con nectors to provide integrations to many third-party solutions that the company wants integrated in to the CMDB. Which categories of connectors are available to the Administrat or? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"DevOps","B":"Cloud","C":"Workflow Automation","D":"Observability"},"answer":"BD"},{"n":71,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"The Server [cmdb_ci_server] class uses a dynamic reconciliation rule of lowest value for the Disk Space (GB) field, while the Windows Server [cmdb_ci_win_server] class uses a dynamic reconciliation rule of most reported for the Disk Space (GB) field. Given the following data sources that populate Windows Server d ata into the CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB: Which value would be added to the CMDB for the Disk Space (GB) field of a Windows Server [cmdb_ci_win_server] record?","choices":{"A":"80","B":"75","C":"50"},"answer":"B"},{"n":72,"domain":"Service Graph Connectors","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager needs to ingest third-party CIs into th e CMDB. Which method minimizes the risk of technical debt?","choices":{"A":"Vendor-provided integration","B":"Table API","C":"Service Graph Connector","D":"Import Sets and Transform Maps"},"answer":"C"},{"n":73,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"Which ServiceNow solutions automatically create relationships b etween CI Applications that are part of an Application Service? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"IntegrationHub ETL","B":"Event Management","C":"Discovery","D":"Service Mapping","E":"Data Manager"},"answer":"CD"},{"n":74,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to leverage dynamic reconciliation r ules. Which feature must be enabled?","choices":{"A":"CMDB Data Manager","B":"CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB","C":"CMDB Workspace","D":"Reconciliation Rules"},"answer":"B"},{"n":75,"domain":"Service Graph Connectors","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator needs the fastest time to value solution f or effectively ingesting, managing, and maintaining CIs and relationships. Which management tool will accomplish this to import Windows co mputer data from SCCM?","choices":{"A":"IntegrationHub ETL connection to SCCM using Robust Transform Engine (RTE)","B":"Import set using JDBC data source connection to SCCM using tr ansform maps","C":"SCCM Service Graph Connector","D":"SCCM Usage Metering Spoke"},"answer":"C"},{"n":76,"domain":"Service Graph Connectors","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator has installed a Service Graph Connector (SGC), and then made customizations to the mappings.Which is a consequence of this action?","choices":{"A":"Fields populated by a customization will have a special tag associated with them in the CMDB.","B":"The customization will prevent the SGC from executing without an approval record attached to the affected mapping record.","C":"The customized mappings are not supported by ServiceNow, and the customer is responsible for supporting their own customized SGC."},"answer":"C"},{"n":77,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Data Owner has requested belter insights on the different data sources that make up the CMDB data set. The Platform Owner knows that the new Service Graph Connector Central plugin is just what is needed.After installing the plugin, what workspace will have the new Service Graph Connector Central tab available?","choices":{"A":"Discovery Admin Workspace","B":"CMDB Workspace","C":"Service Graph Connector Workspace"},"answer":"B"},{"n":78,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"During an automated discovery scan, both a web server instance and its underlying server are detected and ingested into the CMDB. What is the default relationship established between the web server CI and the server CI when both are created in the CMDB?","choices":{"A":"Web Server > Used by::Uses > Server","B":"Web Server > Runs on::Runs > Server","C":"Web Server > Uses::Used by > Server","D":"Web Server > Runs::Runs On > Server"},"answer":"B"},{"n":80,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"Which ServiceNow store application is used to import data from different sources into the CMDB?","choices":{"A":"Service Mapping","B":"Integration Hub ETL","C":"Agent Client Collector"},"answer":"A"},{"n":81,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"The IRE has identified duplicates for one CI. Which will be updated by the IRE?","choices":{"A":"The oldest CI determined by the creation date.","B":"The newest CI determined by the creation date.","C":"The CI with the most recent updated date."},"answer":"A"},{"n":82,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator would like to minimize stale CIs in the CMDB.Which CMDB Health Dashboard scorecard displays this information?","choices":{"A":"Correctness","B":"Compliance","C":"Completeness"},"answer":"A"},{"n":83,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROPDrag and drop the CMDB Health Dashboard metric to the description.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image10.png\">"},{"n":84,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is asked to clean up the CMDB duplicates.What is the preferred way to manage this task?","choices":{"A":"My Tasks in the Application Navigator","B":"The de-duplication task module","C":"The de-duplication dashboard on the CMDB workspace"},"answer":"C"},{"n":85,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator identifies duplicate CIs. One was created by a manual import, and the other one was created by automated discovery. The discovered CI has the latest IP address, while the manually imported CI has an accurate relationship to a critical business application.How does the Administrator use the Duplicate CI Remediator to resolve this issue?","choices":{"A":"Retain the manually imported CI, and delete the discovered CI","B":"Merge the two CIs automatically, retaining all attributes from the discovered CI","C":"Retain the discovered CI, but merge the relationship from the manually imported CI","D":"Retain the discovered CI, and delete the manually imported CI"},"answer":"C"},{"n":86,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to remove all Linux Servers in the organization that have not been updated in six months.Which recommended action does the Administrator take in Data Manager?","choices":{"A":"Create a business rule","B":"Create an archive policy","C":"Create a scheduled job"},"answer":"B"},{"n":87,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"The CMDB Administrator group aims to display meaningful results on the CMDB Health Dashboard Compliance Scorecard for server records that are not on the latest patch.What must be configured to achieve this goal?","choices":{"A":"Certification Policies, Data Filters, Scheduled Jobs","B":"Stale, Orphan, Duplicate","C":"Certification Filter, Certification Template, Audit","D":"Technical Service Offerings, Dynamic CI Groups, CMDB Groups"},"answer":"C"},{"n":88,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator has been tasked with gathering information for a presentation to leadership. The Administrator needs to provide Duplicate CI, Orphan CI, and Stale CI metrics.Which scorecard provides this information on the CMDB Health Dashboard?","choices":{"A":"Completeness","B":"Compliance","C":"Correctness"},"answer":"C"},{"n":89,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"What is the difference between Data Certification and Attestation policies when managing a CI?","choices":{"A":"Attestation requires correcting specific attributes of a CI, while Data Certification tracks acknowledgement the CI still exists.","B":"Attestation can be scheduled, while Data Certification cannot be scheduled.","C":"Attestation tracks acknowledgement the CI still exists, while Data Certification requires validating specific attributes of a CI.","D":"Attestation can be assigned to a Group or an individual, while Data Certification can only be assigned to an individual."},"answer":"C"},{"n":90,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is reviewing the health of the CMDB and notices a large percentage of the Hardware CIs are missing serial numbers. The Administrator is concerned this may cause duplicate CIs and would like to resolve the issue in a timely manner.What structured guidelines provided by ServiceNow are available to troubleshoot and resolve the issue?","choices":{"A":"CMDB Health Dashboards Playbooks","B":"CSDM Now Create Playbooks","C":"CSDB Data Foundations Dashboard Playbooks","D":"CSDM Data Foundations Dashboard Playbooks"},"answer":"C"},{"n":91,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"Configuration Management needs to ensure data quality for all CIs in the CMDB.What areas of data quality for CIs are in the CMDB Health Dashboard? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Missing CIs","B":"State CIs","C":"Duplicate CIs","D":"Downgraded CIs","E":"Upgraded CIs"},"answer":"BC"},{"n":92,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Configuration Manager is reviewing the metrics on the CMDB Health Dashboard’s Correctness Scorecard for the Server class which consists of a total of 60,000 servers in the CMDB.For the Duplicate metric, it shows Healthy CIs/Evaluated as 59,000/60,000.For the Orphan metric, it shows Healthy CIs/Evaluated as 45,000/50,000.Which configuration explains the difference in the scope of Server CIs (60,000 vs.50,000) evaluated between the two metrics?","choices":{"A":"The Duplicate metric has a CMDB Group configured for the Server class.","B":"The Duplicate metric has a Health Inclusion rule configured for the Server class.","C":"The Orphan metric has a Health Inclusion rule configured for the Server class.","D":"The Orphan metric has a CMDB Group configured for the Server class."},"answer":"C"},{"n":93,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"CMDB class owners are receiving tasks under the ‘My Work’ tab in the CMDB Workspace.Which CMDB management tool is generating these tasks?","choices":{"A":"CMDB Data Manager","B":"De-duplication templates","C":"CMDB Health Dashboard"},"answer":"A"},{"n":94,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"What ensures data volume in the CMDB manageable?","choices":{"A":"Scheduled Jobs","B":"Archive Policies","C":"Business Rules"},"answer":"B"},{"n":95,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Manager wants to improve data quality using the CMDB Health Dashboard.What needs to happen to generate CMDB health scores?","choices":{"A":"Nothing, CMDB health scores are calculated by default","B":"The plugin, CMDB health calculation, needs to be installed","C":"The scheduled jobs for the CMDB Health Dashboard must be activated"},"answer":"C"},{"n":96,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"The CMDB Configuration Manager is using the CI Class Manager to manage the group ownership of CI classes and needs to leverage the ownership value specified in the CI Class Manager.When configuring a CMDB Data Manager policy, which group reference field should be set?","choices":{"A":"Change Group","B":"Approval Group","C":"Managed By Group","D":"Support Group"},"answer":"C"},{"n":97,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"The CMDB Configuration Management team wants to manage de-duplication tasks generated from data ingested into the CMDB via the Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE).In which area of the CMDB Workspace can they locate these de-duplication tasks?","choices":{"A":"Important actions tile under the Home tab","B":"CMDB feature adoption tile under the Insight tab","C":"Total status tile under the My Work tab"},"answer":"A"},{"n":98,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"Which type of CMDB Data Manager policy creates tasks that allow the assigned individual to update fields on the CI record?","choices":{"A":"Compliance","B":"Certification","C":"Attestation","D":"Audit"},"answer":"B"},{"n":99,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROPA new ServiceNow customer is assembling a Configuration Management team to support their CMDB.Drag each role to its corresponding job description.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image12.png\">"},{"n":100,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROPA CMDB Administrator seeks to understand the available tools for preventing, addressing, and remediating duplicate CIs.Drag and drop each feature with the corresponding outcome.Some options may not apply.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image14.png\">"},{"n":101,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager needs to leverage a policy type to automate the creation and assignment of tasks to validate the existence of CIs.Which policy type should be used to accomplish this goal?","choices":{"A":"Retire","B":"Certification","C":"Delete","D":"Attestation"},"answer":"D"},{"n":102,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"Which is a purpose or requirement of CMDB Data Manager in ServiceNow?","choices":{"A":"Encrypts archived records for enhanced security","B":"Automates the enforcement of relationship rules between CIs in the CMDB","C":"Automates the archival and deletion of records based on retention policies"},"answer":"C"},{"n":103,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Data Manager needs to access the ServiceNow platform to create, publish, and manage policies that automate and govern CI lifecycle operations, ensuring the CMDB remains healthy and efficient.Where can the Data Manager do this?","choices":{"A":"CMDB Workspace Management tab","B":"Service Operations Workspace","C":"CMDB Workspace CMDB 360 tab","D":"CI Class Manager"},"answer":"A"},{"n":104,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to ensure all short-lived CIs that have not been discovered in the past week are removed.After retiring the CI records, which recommended action does the CMDB Administrator take?","choices":{"A":"Create a delete police","B":"Create a business rule","C":"Create a scheduled job"},"answer":"C"},{"n":105,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator has taken over management of a ServiceNow instance and has determined there are multiple deficiencies in the CMDB. During review of the CMDB Data Foundations Dashboard, the Administrator sees that ServiceNow offers Remediation Playbooks.How can Playbooks assist the Administrator in resolving these issues?","choices":{"A":"Playbooks can be installed in the instance to automatically fix issues.","B":"Playbooks can help analyze and fix issues.","C":"Playbooks can automatically track common CMDB issues and output metrics."},"answer":"B"},{"n":106,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator utilizing the CMDB Data Foundations Dashboard sees an issue and wants to run a playbook.Which types of documentation can they expect to be provided in a playbook? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Root Cause","B":"Automated Remediations","C":"Problem Analysis","D":"Problem Overview"},"answer":"CD"},{"n":107,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is considering whether to start using the playbooks provided on the CMDB Data Foundation Dashboard. What are the benefits to support the decision to leverage this feature? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Offers automated scripts to resolve poorly performing metrics","B":"Offers insight into the downstream impacts of poorly performing metrics","C":"Offers remediation options to address and improve poorly performing metrics","D":"Offers remediation templates to improve poorly performing metrics"},"answer":"BC"},{"n":108,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is beginning the journey of populating the CMDB and needs to verify that any data which is no longer useful/applicable is removed. Which governance management tool will accomplish this?","choices":{"A":"CI Class Manager","B":"CMDB and CSDM Data Foundations Dashboard","C":"CMDB Data Manager","D":"De-duplication Templates","E":"CMDB Health Dashboard"},"answer":"C"},{"n":109,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"The CMDB Administrator wants to leverage the Staleness metric from the CMDB Health Dashboard - Correctness Scorecard.Which field is used to calculate the duration of this metric?","choices":{"A":"Updated (sys_updated_on)","B":"Created (sys_created_on)","C":"Last modified on (last_modified)","D":"Most recent discovery (last_discovery)","E":"First discovered (first_discovered)"},"answer":"A"},{"n":110,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A data center has many servers. The CMDB Administrator wants to confirm that all servers exist.Which Data Manager policy type does the Administrator implement?","choices":{"A":"Attestation","B":"Certification","C":"Promotion","D":"Verification"},"answer":"A"},{"n":111,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"Using existing baseline Data Manager policies, what condition must a CI meet before it can be archived or deleted?","choices":{"A":"Be fully operational and in use","B":"Be marked as critical","C":"Be retired and in end of life","D":"Be marked as inactive"},"answer":"C"},{"n":112,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"The Configuration Management team wants to confirm that all servers in the CMDB actually exist in the data center.Which CMDB Data Manager policy type would the team create?","choices":{"A":"Attestation","B":"Retire","C":"Delete","D":"Archive","E":"Certification"},"answer":"A"},{"n":113,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROP-Drag and drop the CMDB Health Dashboard metric to the description.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image25.png\">"},{"n":114,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROP-The CMDB Health Dashboard is based on three Key Performance Indicators (KPIs): Correctness, Compliance, and Completeness. Each KPI includes several sub-metrics.Drag the sub-metrics to the KPI.Some options may not apply.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image27.png\">"},{"n":115,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"How do CMDB management tools and features within the CMDB gover nance pillar help organizations manage CIs and improve service delivery? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Reduced hardware costs","B":"Gain visibility and control","C":"Assist integration choices","D":"Enhanced Service Management operations"},"answer":"BD"},{"n":116,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"What types of policies can be created within CMDB Data Manager? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Retire","B":"Reconciliation","C":"De-duplication","D":"Archive"},"answer":"AD"},{"n":117,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"Which default user groups are available when setting up a CMDB Data Manager policy and specifying the task assignment with the Assignment type set to 'User Group Field'? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Owned by Group","B":"Assignment Group","C":"Managed By Group","D":"Support Group"},"answer":"CD"},{"n":118,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"During a CMDB implementation, a team member is tasked with ensu ring the accuracy and completeness of CI data. This person is also responsible for maintaining dat a quality and resolving discrepancies. Which role is responsible for these tasks?","choices":{"A":"CMDB Architect","B":"IT Asset Manager","C":"Configuration Manager","D":"Service Owner"},"answer":"C"},{"n":119,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Configuration Manager sets up the following data filter for a certification policy using CMDB Data Manager. ● Table: Server [cmdb_ci_server] ● Filter: Operating System | cont ains | Server OR Operating Sy stem | contains | Linux Which operating systems are affected by this policy? (Choose tw o.)","choices":{"A":"Linux CentOS","B":"AIX","C":"Windows Server 2022 Datacenter","D":"Windows 2019 Datacenter"},"answer":"AC"},{"n":120,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator needs to track which CIs and CI classes ar e missing key data. Which CMDB Health Dashboard scorecard supports tracking this re quirement?","choices":{"A":"Correctness","B":"Completeness","C":"Compliance"},"answer":"B"},{"n":121,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator has a number of similar de-duplication tas ks that need to be remediated in bulk. How does the Administrator achieve this?","choices":{"A":"Utilize the Duplicate CI Remediator Wizard","B":"Configure and run a custom de-duplication background script","C":"Create de-duplication tasks manually and remediate each","D":"Create and run a de-duplication template"},"answer":"D"},{"n":122,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator group aims to establish a process for rece iving task notifications when the Support Group or Managed By Group fields are not populated for operatio nal Linux servers stored in the CMDB. Which ServiceNow modules can be leveraged to configure recommen ded fields and generate task records in cases where these fields are missing for Linux servers in th e CMDB?","choices":{"A":"CMDB Workspace and Scheduled Jobs","B":"Technical Service Offerings and Dynamic CI groups","C":"Dynamic CI groups and CMDB groups","D":"CI Class Manager and Health Preferences"},"answer":"D"},{"n":123,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator has a report in ServiceNow that lists all CMDB Services that do not have an owner and wants to use a ServiceNow Playbook. What Governance process play can prevent this from recurring?","choices":{"A":"Set a default value on the Service Owner field so that is nev er empty","B":"Make the field Owned by mandatory","C":"Make the field Managed by mandatory on all CIs"},"answer":"B"},{"n":124,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to leverage the Staleness metric from the CMDB Health Dashboard - Correctness Scorecard.What is the default duration of this metric?","choices":{"A":"30 days","B":"24 hours","C":"7 days","D":"60 days"},"answer":"D"},{"n":125,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager responsible for a specific region wants to use the CMDB Health Dashboard to improve the data quality of the CMDB for that region. The Configuration Manager only sees the overall score and grouped by CI Class.How can the Configuration Manager get a score for regionally relevant CIs?","choices":{"A":"On the CMDB health settings, activate the option, Group scores by region","B":"Customize the CMDB Health Dashboard scheduled jobs to group the results by region","C":"Create CMDB groups with type, health, by region"},"answer":"C"},{"n":126,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"How does a CMDB Administrator use the ServiceNow Platform to ensure the data quality associated with CIs in the CMDB?","choices":{"A":"Data Quality Scheduled Job","B":"CMDB Audit Business Rule","C":"CMDB Workspace","D":"Data Quality Business Rule"},"answer":"D"},{"n":127,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Configuration Manager is reviewing the metrics on the CM DB Health Dashboard's Correctness Scorecard. For the Duplicate metric in the Server class, it sho ws Healthy CIs/Evaluated as 59,000/60,000. What does this indicate about the scope of server records calcu lated under this metric?","choices":{"A":"1,000 server records are in scope for this metric","B":"60,000 server records are in scope for this metric","C":"59,000 Linux and 60,000 Windows servers records are in scope for this metric","D":"59,000 server records are in scope for this metric"},"answer":"B"},{"n":128,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to start utilizing the CMDB Health D ashboard and its Key Performance Indicators. What does the Administrator do to start using the dashboard?","choices":{"A":"Download the dashboard from the ServiceNow store","B":"Nothing, the dashboard is activated by default","C":"Activate the dashboard scheduled jobs","D":"Activate the dashboard system property"},"answer":"C"},{"n":129,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"Which are CMDB Data Manager end of life policy types? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Archive","B":"Retire","C":"Lost","D":"Decommission","E":"Disposed"},"answer":"AB"},{"n":130,"domain":"Service Graph Connectors","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB team has noticed that some hardware CIs are missing the serial number information, making it difficult to maintain data accuracy. The team needs a structure d approach to identify and address these gaps. Which accomplishes this task?","choices":{"A":"CI Class Manager","B":"Service Graph Connectors","C":"CMDB Data Foundation Playbook"},"answer":"C"},{"n":131,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Configuration Manager intends to implement CMDB Data Man ager delete and archive policies for all server records in the New York datacenter. In which lifecycle state would servers be affected by these new policies?","choices":{"A":"Missing - Stolen","B":"Inventory - Available","C":"End of Life - Retired","D":"In any lifecycle stale"},"answer":"C"},{"n":132,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"The CMDB Administrator has been asked to establish Configuratio n Management with a functional CMDB. Which factor is most critical for successfully operationalizing the CMDB in ServiceNow?","choices":{"A":"Populating the CMDB with as much data as possible to ensure a comprehensive inventory of CIs","B":"Establishing clear governance and continuously monitoring CMD B health","C":"Allowing IT teams to modify CMDB records as needed to promote flexibility in data management","D":"Relying on automated discovery tools to maintain and update C MDB records"},"answer":"B"},{"n":133,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"Where does a user with the appropriate role(s) review and manage the generated tasks after configuring CMDB Data Manager policies?","choices":{"A":"CMDB Health Dashboard > Duplicate CIs tab","B":"CMDB Workspace > My Work tab","C":"CMDB Health Dashboard > Audit tab","D":"CMDB Workspace > Management tab"},"answer":"B"},{"n":134,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Management Process Owner needs to configure Dat a Manager for policy tasks to be correctly assigned and aligned with the group attribute assigne d to a class in CI Class Manager. Which is the recommended field to be used for a policy task ass ignment?","choices":{"A":"Managed by group","B":"Change group","C":"Approval group","D":"Support group"},"answer":"A"},{"n":135,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator uses the CMDB Data Foundations Dashboard t o gain insights into the CMDB. The results display low scores for several metrics. Which actions can the CMDB Administrator take to improve the CM DB Health? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Remove non-operational and retired CIs","B":"Focus on metric(s) with Critical and High priorities","C":"Adjust the metrics using exclusion rules to improve the score s","D":"Use the Remediation Playbooks linked beside each metric"},"answer":"BD"},{"n":136,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"Which shows the most complete list of policy types that are pro vided by the CMDB Data Manager?","choices":{"A":"Delete, Attestation, Retire, and Certification","B":"Attestation, Retire, and Certification","C":"Archive and Delete","D":"Retire, Archive, Attestation, Certification, and Delete"},"answer":"D"},{"n":137,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"The CMDB Administrator group seeks to filler specific CI classe s that display on the CMDB Health Dashboard. This ensures that only relevant data is displayed, e xcluding items that are not ready for management. Which feature can the group utilize to achieve this goal?","choices":{"A":"Reconciliation Rules","B":"Identification Rules","C":"Data Refresh Rules","D":"Health Inclusion Rules"},"answer":"D"},{"n":138,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is using the Duplicate CI Remediator to ad dress a de-duplication task. On the first lab of the wizard, the Main CI is selected. Which attributes are used to identify the Main CI? (Choose two. )","choices":{"A":"Least Related Items","B":"Most Related Items","C":"Newest Created","D":"Oldest Created"},"answer":"BD"},{"n":139,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager needs to enable a CMDB Data Manager pol icy to remove records from a CI Class while retaining the ability to restore them within a spec ified period. Which policy type should the Configuration Manager create?","choices":{"A":"Archive","B":"Retire","C":"Certification","D":"Delete"},"answer":"A"},{"n":140,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"Which roles are assigned to a user to either configure or work on tasks generated by CMDB Data Manager? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"cmdb dm admin","B":"data manager user","C":"cmdb_dm_user","D":"data_manager_admin"},"answer":"B"},{"n":144,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"The life cycle sync is enabled on a ServiceNow instance. The ITAM Administrator sets the state of a set of servers to retired. What is the out of the box life cycle stage value of the CIs associated with the assets?","choices":{"A":"End of operation","B":"Disposed","C":"End of life"},"answer":"C"},{"n":150,"domain":"Data Sources & Ingestion","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Management Process Owner is planning to deploy a ServiceNow CMDB and aims to minimize the risk of technical debt. Which pillars of a successful data foundation will accomplish this? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Insight","B":"Govern","C":"Ingest","D":"Plan"},"answer":"B"},{"n":151,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROPA manufacturing organization has implemented Incident Management in ServiceNow and wants to integrate additional products to enhance its functionality.Drag each ServiceNow product to the value it brings to supporting Incident Management.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image16.png\">"},{"n":152,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"Where can a CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB Saved Query be viewed and created in the CMDB Workspace?","choices":{"A":"Saved queries window on the Insight tab","B":"CMDB Query Builder","C":"Coverage window on the CMDB 360 tab","D":"Saved queries window on the CMDB 360 tab"},"answer":"D"},{"n":153,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"An organization is changing data centers and needs to know the consequences of the planned changes.How can Application Service mapping be used as part of Change Management?","choices":{"A":"To understand the physical location of CIs","B":"To identify which devices will go offline first","C":"To understand the business impact of CIs"},"answer":"C"},{"n":154,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"Where can an administrator perform Natural Language Queries (NLQ)?","choices":{"A":"CMDB Data Manager","B":"CI Class Manager","C":"CMDB Workspace","D":"CMDB Health Dashboard"},"answer":"C"},{"n":155,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A healthcare provider faces a critical incident affecting its patient management system. The provider needs to determine the users impacted to mitigate disruption effectively.Which CSDM-related data should they leverage?","choices":{"A":"Incident history of similar CIs","B":"Application Service environment attribute","C":"Service Offerings by Department or Location","D":"Affected CI [task_ci] related list"},"answer":"C"},{"n":156,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager wants to use the Unified Map.Where would it be accessed?","choices":{"A":"CMDB Data Manager","B":"CI Class Manager","C":"CMDB Workspace"},"answer":"C"},{"n":157,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"A service owner is using Unified Map to understand to composition of a service but wants to filter out irrelevant information.Which options are available to the service owner from the filter panel? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Discovery source","B":"CI type","C":"Business critically","D":"Managed by group"},"answer":"AB"},{"n":158,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to create a CMDB query to find all databases located in Seattle that are connected to application services. They also want to include incidents related to those databases.Which actions does the company take to build this query? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Add to the canvas the Incident table from the Non-CMDB Tables list","B":"Add a filter to the database node for location=Seattle","C":"Set the relationship level to ‘Up to 2nd level relationships’","D":"Add property columns to the application service node"},"answer":"AB"},{"n":159,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"The Configuration Management team finds value in the reports fr om CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB and wants to use it for all CI data. Which must be true in order for CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB to be able to report on and analyze that data?","choices":{"A":"Reconciliation rules with priorities must be configured.","B":"The CI data must be from an authorized Service Graph Connecto r.","C":"The CI data must go through the IRE.","D":"ServiceNow Discovery must be used to populate the CI data."},"answer":"C"},{"n":160,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"ServiceNow Event Management significantly benefits from a well- maintained and properly populated CMDB. What are key advantages it provides to Event Management? (Choos e two.)","choices":{"A":"Correlation of alerts to knowledge base articles","B":"Mapped services provide visibility to the business impact of an alert","C":"Binding of alerts to specific CIs","D":"Mapped services provide visibility to users consuming the ser vice"},"answer":"BC"},{"n":161,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator needs insights into how their CMDB is conf igured according to ServiceNow recommended practice. Which should be used?","choices":{"A":"CMDB Health Dashboard","B":"CMDB Workspace","C":"CMDB Data Manager","D":"CMDB Data Foundation Dashboard"},"answer":"D"},{"n":162,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"What is the value of using the CMDB in security operations? (Ch oose two.)","choices":{"A":"Auto-resolves a vulnerability","B":"Identifies the IT infrastructure with a vulnerability","C":"Enables audits and attestations across CIs","D":"Allows security team to assess and remediate an incident"},"answer":"BD"},{"n":163,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"The CMDB Configuration Management team has successfully develop ed a healthy and trusted CMDB. They have integrated discovered infrastructure data, accurately referenced non-discoverable data (such as change and support group information), and made the CMDB servic e-aware using Service Mapping. How will these improvements enhance the change management proce ss? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Provides insight into the potential impact of the change","B":"Ensures that no changes result in service downtime, regardles s of planning or execution","C":"Automatically schedules and deploys changes without human rev iew or approval","D":"Enables auto population of the assignment group field to dyna mically route changes"},"answer":"AD"},{"n":164,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Manager uses CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB to maintain and i mprove CMDB quality. Why would the Manager use CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB?","choices":{"A":"To identify CI attributes from multiple data sources","B":"To ingest data from multiple data sources using Import Set(s)","C":"To populate the CMDB from multiple data sources","D":"To ingest data from multiple data sources using Service Graph Connector(s)"},"answer":"A"},{"n":165,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is comparing the Unified Map to the Service Mapping map.What are additional capabilities of the Unified Map? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Number of levels displayed on a map can be modified","B":"Visibility to an application and the host it is installed on","C":"Map nodes can be filtered based on user preferences","D":"Map can be zoomed in and out"},"answer":"CD"},{"n":166,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A Service Desk Manager wants to leverage the Unified Map to fin d active incidents or problems for a selected CI. Which panel will give the manager visibility and details?","choices":{"A":"Overview","B":"Attributes","C":"Related items","D":"Application services"},"answer":"C"},{"n":167,"domain":"Discovery & MID Server","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to educate the team on the various actions that can be performed within the CMDB Workspace.What actions can be initiated from the CMDB Workspace? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Create a new CMDB class","B":"Execute ServiceNow Discovery","C":"Remediate duplicate CI records","D":"Create a CMDB Data Manager certification policy"},"answer":"BC"},{"n":168,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator knows that the CMDB Data Foundation Dashbo ard is a resource to monitor and improve data quality. What is a benefit of this dashboard?","choices":{"A":"Provides the ability to resolve certification policy tasks","B":"Provides the ability to configure health-related metrics","C":"Provides key health-related metrics to make decisions"},"answer":"C"},{"n":169,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is asked to create a query using the CMDB Query Builder that displays all operational CIs belonging to a specific application service. Which steps provide the desired outcome?","choices":{"A":"1. Add the Business Application, Application Service, and Con figuration Item classes to the canvas. 2. Define a filter for the application service name and the ope rational status of the configuration items. 3. Configure the relationship between the classes. 4. Run the query.","B":"1. Add the Application Service and Configuration Item classes to the canvas. 2. Configure the relationship between the classes. 3. Define a filter for the application service name and the ope rational status of the configuration items. 4. Run the query.","C":"1. Add the Application Service and Configuration Item classes to the canvas. 2. Configure the relationship between the classes. 3. Add the Operational Status and Name fields as columns. 4. Run the query."},"answer":"B"},{"n":170,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager wants to explore ServiceNow CMDB 360 sa ved queries to see if the reports can assist with managing of CMDB data. What insights are gained from CMDB 360 queries? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Gaps in attribute data from different data sources","B":"Unique CIs created from different data sources","C":"Different attribute values from different data sources","D":"Orphan CIs created from different data sources","E":"Duplicate configuration items from different data sources"},"answer":"AC"},{"n":171,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to leverage the CMDB Data Foundations Dashboard.What are benefits of using this application?","choices":{"A":"Checks that important data is valid and properly configured","B":"Has a framework to create custom metrics for the CMDB","C":"Provides playbooks to assist in the remediation of potential risks","D":"Uses automation to remediate potential risks"},"answer":"AC"},{"n":172,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A Service Owner needs to view related items, such as Active Inc idents and Planned Changes, directly on the home node of the Unified Map. Which work area would allow the Service Owner to meet this goal ?","choices":{"A":"Map","B":"Tool box","C":"Content controls","D":"Contextual side panel"},"answer":"D"},{"n":173,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to use the CMDB and CSDM Data Founda tions Dashboard. Where can the Administrator obtain the dashboard?","choices":{"A":"It is a free application on the ServiceNow Innovation Lab.","B":"It is active by default.","C":"It is a free application on the ServiceNow Store.","D":"It is a paid application on the ServiceNow Store."},"answer":"C"},{"n":174,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager working in the CMDB Workspace wants to see how CIs are connected to each other. Which tool can be used?","choices":{"A":"Relationship Map","B":"Business Service Map","C":"Unified Map"},"answer":"C"},{"n":175,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"An organization is using CMDB Query Builder to find all applica tion services with a database that has incidents and all infrastructure in those application services. Which steps does the organization take to build this query? (Ch oose two.)","choices":{"A":"Use a CMDB Query to include application services and their re lated infrastructure","B":"Use a Service Mapping Query to find all incidents related to the database","C":"Use a Service Mapping Query to include non-CMDB tables like t he Incident table","D":"Add a non-CMDB table to the query"},"answer":"AD"},{"n":182,"domain":"CI Classes & Schema","ctx":-1,"q":"Where can a CMDB 360 saved query be created?","choices":{"A":"CI Class Manager","B":"CMDB Reports","C":"CMDB Workspace","D":"CMDB Query Builder"},"answer":"C"},{"n":183,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"In a company there is a need to understand the CSDM maturity level needed. Different stakeholders listed a number of use cases that they expect over time.Which use case requires information objects?","choices":{"A":"The Event Operations team wants to automate their events into incident for operational actions.","B":"The Business Service Management team wants to understand the operational impact for their consumer parties.","C":"The Customer Service team wants to onboard pro-active case management.","D":"The SecOps team wants to understand the operational risk in the Business Application context.","E":"The Asset Management wants to understand to asset life cycle compliancy in a Business Application context."},"answer":"D"},{"n":184,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A Platform Owner is collaborating with stakeholders in the manufacturing industry to align their CIs with the CSDM 5 framework. They need to map production line monitoring systems to the appropriate CSDM domain.Which CSDM 5 domain does the Platform Owner use?","choices":{"A":"Build and Integration (Build)","B":"Service Delivery (Manage Technical)","C":"Service Consumption (Sell/Consume)","D":"Design and Planning (Design)","E":"Foundation"},"answer":"B"},{"n":185,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A development team is working on a project and an application will be deployed to many servers. There will be several security requirements that must be checked to adhere to lawful compliance because the application will be holding customer personal data (PII and PCI).Where in the CSDM does the development team look to store the information that will be used to satisfy the audits?","choices":{"A":"Technology Management Service Offerings (Technical Service Offerings) and Dynamic CI Groups","B":"Business Applications and Information Objects","C":"Customer Service Offerings and Databases"},"answer":"B"},{"n":186,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A customer’s CMDB is aligned to the CSDM Walk stage.What benefit is provided by the CMDB?","choices":{"A":"Enables impact assessments for incident, problem, and change on Business Services","B":"Improves the implementation velocity of APM Foundation for future business application rationalization","C":"Allows for additional stratification of Technical team’s support structure along the lines of OLAs and commitments"},"answer":"C"},{"n":187,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"Some steps need to be taken to transition from using legacy CMDB status attributes to CSDM lifecycle objects. Drag and drop the objects / attributes to the correct descriptions.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image18.png\">"},{"n":188,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to improve data quality related to the CSDM.Which action should the Administrator take to meet this goal?","choices":{"A":"Use the default configured CMDB Health Dashboard","B":"Start the ServiceNow Health Scan","C":"Use the CSDM Data Foundation Dashboard"},"answer":"C"},{"n":189,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"According to the Common Service Data Model (CSDM), a server team is requesting a catalog item be created for infrastructure upgrade requests.Which role is involved in initiating the request and defining requirements?","choices":{"A":"Enterprise Architecture","B":"Technology Service Owners","C":"Application Service Owners"},"answer":"B"},{"n":190,"domain":"IRE & Identification","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is evaluating whether to monitor the metrics provided on the CMDB Foundation Dashboard.Which benefits support the decision to continually monitor the results on this dashboard? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Provides a list of all CIs that failed health audits","B":"Provides metrics for CIs Processed by the IRE","C":"Provides metrics on active CIs updated in the last 90 days","D":"Reports on all orphan CIs in the CMDB"},"answer":"BC"},{"n":191,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"The Configuration Manager is preparing the justification to utilize the CMDB Data Foundations Dashboard.Which benefits align with the usage of this dashboard? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"It enables monitoring and tracking of CMDB health over time.","B":"It provides actionable insights to improve data quality and completeness.","C":"It helps detect and eliminate duplicate records in the CMDB.","D":"It automates the approval process for change management."},"answer":"AB"},{"n":192,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A Change Manager wants to gain value from CSDM.How will the Change Management process benefit from CSDM? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Identify blackout windows for the change","B":"Determine the root cause of the change issue","C":"Understand the impact of the change on services","D":"Route the change dynamically"},"answer":"CD"},{"n":193,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"Which are business values of CMDB? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Collecting and managing financial data","B":"Streaming incident and change management","C":"Strengthening operational resiliency","D":"Automating maintenance for CI relationships"},"answer":"BC"},{"n":194,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is implementing a Vulnerability Response or Security Incident Response and needs to ensure customers have enough context to estimate risk and set task priorities.Which Get Well Playbook from the CSDM Data Foundation Dashboard helps with this?","choices":{"A":"Locations without a Parent Location","B":"Named Product Models without Product Owners","C":"Percentage of Custom Status Values for CI Life Cycle Stages","D":"Application Services with Business Application Relationships"},"answer":"D"},{"n":195,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to run the Services Have Owners Identified playbook to remediate the issues shown in the CMDB Data Foundations Dashboard.Which remediation plays would be used? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Govern Data","B":"Fix Data","C":"Report Data","D":"Analyze Data"},"answer":"BD"},{"n":196,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Management Governance team is transitioning from utilizing legacy CMDB status fields to CSDM life cycle status fields.Which table can be modified?","choices":{"A":"Life Cycle Stages [life_cycle_stage]","B":"Life Cycle Mapping [life_cycle_mapping]","C":"Life Cycle Controls [life_cycle_control]","D":"Life Cycle Stage Status [life_cycle_stage_status]"},"answer":"B"},{"n":197,"domain":"CMDB Health","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator, viewing the CMDB Data Foundations Dashboard, notices the Unique Locations Result percentage low.What is the recommended process from the associated playbook to correct this issue?","choices":{"A":"Review both locations, update CIs with the correct location and delete the duplicate location","B":"Retain the location that matches the organization’s standard naming convention, and delete the duplicate without further validation","C":"Keep both locations as either can be used as a valid alternate location","D":"Use the Duplicate CI Remediator the merge the duplicate location records"},"answer":"A"},{"n":198,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROPA CMDB Owner starts on the CSDM journey and needs to become familiar with the CSDM domains.Drag the CMDB objects to the correct CSDM domains.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image20.png\">"},{"n":199,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager is planning the implementation of the CMDB.Which is the prescribed CSDM rollout order?","choices":{"A":"Architecture, Business, Technical, Governance","B":"Initiate, Plan, Execute, Deliver, Close","C":"Foundation, Crawl, Walk, Run, Fly","D":"Initial, Developing, Defined, Managed"},"answer":"C"},{"n":200,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"A customer wants to model their business applications and would like to capture different types of data that includes Personally Identifiable Information (PII) data. Based on these requirements, which CMDB class needs to be leveraged to achieve this?","choices":{"A":"API Component","B":"Information Object","C":"Business Capability","D":"Data Classification"},"answer":"B"},{"n":201,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A CSDM Data Manager needs metrics on the alignment of product m odels, locations, and business units with best practices. Which tab in the CSDM Data Foundations Dashboard provides this information?","choices":{"A":"Fly","B":"Crawl","C":"Foundation","D":"Run","E":"Walk"},"answer":"C"},{"n":202,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A Service Portfolio Manager wants to know what Application Services their Business Service Offerings depend on.What stage of CSDM would map this relationship?","choices":{"A":"Foundation","B":"Fly","C":"Run","D":"Walk","E":"Crawl"},"answer":"D"},{"n":203,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"An Enterprise Architect of a financial services company is work ing across the enterprise and wants to track their capabilities. Which CSDM 5 domain is used?","choices":{"A":"Build and Integration (Build)","B":"Design and Planning (Design)","C":"Service Delivery (Manage Technical)","D":"Service Consumption (Sell/Consume)","E":"Foundation"},"answer":"B"},{"n":204,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROP Given a list of Service types in the platform. Drag the appropriate service to its definition.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image29.png\">"},{"n":205,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROP A Platform Owner is building the governance team to support the CSDM. Drag the domain to the roles that make up the governance team.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image31.png\">"},{"n":206,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"DRAG DROP An Enterprise Architect needs to help the CMDB owner understand the benefits of CSDM. Drag the CSDM domains to the respective benefits.","visual":true,"choices":{},"answer":"","answerHtml":"<img src=\"https://img.itexams.com/cis-df/image33.png\">"},{"n":207,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A health organization must track certain data (for example, reg ulated patient information) and its relation to Business Applications. Which action does CSDM recommend to meet this goal?","choices":{"A":"Create fields on the Business Application record to mark the Business Application as containing patient information, and then ask the Business Application owner to mark the application as having patient information or not.","B":"Work with the Database administration team to classify the data on each database that holds patient information, and then use Relationships to map that back to the Business Application.","C":"Create an information Object to represent the patient information, and then link it through a relationship to the Business Application after consulting with the Application owner."},"answer":"C"},{"n":208,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Architect intends to populate the CMDB using the CSDM gu idance. Which key stakeholders from the organization should be involved in decisions regarding population of the CMDB using the CSDM Crawl Stage?","choices":{"A":"Business Service Manager, Technology Service Owner","B":"Application Owner, Application Service Owner","C":"Customer Service Manager, Infrastructure Manager"},"answer":"B"},{"n":209,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A hospital has received a new CT Scanner. The inventory managem ent team has created a catalog item doctors can use to schedule patients for scans. What CSDM domain should the inventory management team map the c atalog item to?","choices":{"A":"Foundation","B":"Design and Planning (Design)","C":"Service Delivery (Manage Technical Service)","D":"Service Consumption (Sell/Consume)","E":"Build and Integration (Build)"},"answer":"D"},{"n":210,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A CSDM Data Manager needs metrics on the alignment of Technology Management Services (Technical Services) and Technology Management Offerings (Technical Service Offerings) with best practices.Which tab in the CSDM Data Foundation Dashboard provides this information?","choices":{"A":"Crawl","B":"Run","C":"Walk","D":"Fly"},"answer":"C"},{"n":211,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Architect intends to build a CMDB using CSDM guidance. Which CMDB tables will the architect use to build the CSDM sell /consume domain?","choices":{"A":"Business Capability, Information Object, Business Application","B":"Business Service Offering, Business Service","C":"Application Service, Technology Management Service (Technical Service), Technology Management Offering (Technical Service Offering)"},"answer":"B"},{"n":212,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"The Application Portfolio Management team is asking for help modeling platforms as Business Applications.How would this be mapped in CSDM using the ServiceNow Platform in the Incident and Change applications?","choices":{"A":"ServiceNow Platform, Incident, and Change would all be web based Architecture type.Incident and Change would have a reference to ServiceNow Platform.","B":"ServiceNow Platform would be an Architecture type of Platform Host.Incident and Change would be Platform Applications and have a reference to ServiceNow Platform.","C":"ServiceNow Platform, Incident, and Change would all be web based Architecture type.A Depends On relationship would be created between ServiceNow Platform and Incident and Change.","D":"ServiceNow Platform would be an Architecture type of Platform Host.Incident and Change would be Platform Applications.Then a Depends On relationship would be created between ServiceNow Platform and Incident and Change."},"answer":"B"},{"n":213,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A Manager needs information on how to correctly establish relat ionships between Infrastructure CIs, Technology Management Offerings (Technical Service Offerings), and Application Services within the CMDB. Which CSDM domain would provide this information?","choices":{"A":"Design and Planning (Design)","B":"Service Consumption (Sell / Consume)","C":"Service Delivery (Manage Technical Services)","D":"Build and Integration (Build)","E":"Foundation"},"answer":"C"},{"n":214,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A retail organization needs to ensure that incidents affecting customer-facing services are resolved quickly to reduce potential revenue loss. Which CSDM attribute is used to prioritize these services?","choices":{"A":"Assignment Group on the CI record","B":"Affected CIs in the Incident record","C":"Business Criticality in the Service Offering","D":"Service classification in the Technical Service"},"answer":"C"},{"n":215,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Manager wants to start adding CSDM design and planning (design) domain components into the CMDB.Who is involved in this exercise? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Application Service Owner","B":"Enterprise Architect","C":"Business Relationship Manager","D":"Application Owner"},"answer":"BD"},{"n":216,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A company wants to track regulatory compliance. ServiceNow has an artifact type called an information object as part of the CSDM framework. What is the purpose of an information object?","choices":{"A":"It describes data in general on a group of Configuration Item s.","B":"It describes data exchanged between an API interface and an A pplication.","C":"It describes the logical data to the Business Applications."},"answer":"C"},{"n":217,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"The ITSM Manager wants to use Technology Management Offerings (Technical Service Offerings) to populate the support group of associated CIs.What CSDM stage would this be completed in?","choices":{"A":"Run","B":"Walk","C":"Foundation","D":"Fly","E":"Crawl"},"answer":"B"},{"n":218,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager is implementing end to end service mode ling and wants to get help on status and playbooks for improving the quality. What does the Configuration Manager reference to obtain guidanc e?","choices":{"A":"CMDB Data Foundation Dashboard","B":"Service Mapping Data Foundation Dashboard","C":"CSDM Data Foundation Dashboard","D":"CMDB Workspace"},"answer":"C"},{"n":219,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is leveraging CI data as part of an Integr ated Risk Management implementation and the Entity Scoping process. The Administrator wants to leve rage the CSDM Data Foundations Dashboard playbooks under the Run tab. Which CSDM relationships are leveraged using the CSDM playbooks ? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Business Applications that have their relationships to Inform ation Objects","B":"Business Applications that have relationships to Application Services","C":"Logical CIs that have relationships with Information Objects","D":"Locations that have established parent records"},"answer":"AB"},{"n":220,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"The Incident Process Owner asks which classes of CSDM are used on the Incident form. Which classes are appropriate? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Application Service","B":"Service Offering","C":"Business Application","D":"Service Portfolio"},"answer":"AB"},{"n":221,"domain":"CSDM","ctx":-1,"q":"A Business Relationship Manager in an organization wants to imp lement Service Portfolio Management (SPM) and to present offerings to business consumers. Which CSDM Domain does this align with?","choices":{"A":"Design and Planning (Design)","B":"Service Consumption (Sell/Consume)","C":"Service Delivery","D":"Build and Integration (Build)"},"answer":"B"},{"n":222,"domain":"CMDB Core & Data Foundations","ctx":-1,"q":"How is the CMDB aligned to business processes? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Enables the CFO/CIO to track software licenses","B":"Enhances decision-making and operational efficiency across th e organization","C":"Extends service delivery management to all enterprise departm ents","D":"Provides a centralized view of configuration items and their relationships"},"answer":"BD"},{"n":223,"domain":"Service Mapping","ctx":-1,"q":"A company has recently acquired another company and would like to unify their deployed applications in ServiceNow. Which CSDM record type will help achieve this?","choices":{"A":"Business Application [cmdb_ci_business_app]","B":"Application [cmdb_ci_appl]","C":"Incident [incident]","D":"Application Service [cmdb ci service auto]"},"answer":"A"},{"n":224,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager must use a policy type to automatically create and assign tasks that verify the existence of CIs. \\ \\ Which policy type should be used to meet this goal?","choices":{"A":"Retire","B":"Certification","C":"Delete","D":"Attestation"},"answer":"D","exp":"An Attestation policy assigns tasks for users to verify the physical existence of the IT infrastructure or applications represented by CIs. Certification is used to verify specified data attributes, whereas Retire and Delete govern CI lifecycle actions.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [Working with CMDB Data Manager](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/en-US/bundle/zurich-servicenow-platform/page/product/configuration-management/concept/cmdb-data-management.html) · [CMDB Data Manager experience in CMDB Workspace and in Service Graph Workspace](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/data-mgr-exp-cmdb-workspace.html)"},{"n":225,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"Some steps are required to transition from different CMDB status attributes to life-cycle objects. \\ \\ Drag the objectives or attributes to their matching descriptions.","choices":{},"answer":"","exp":"A lifecycle stage records the high-level phase of a CI’s lifecycle, and lifecycle stage status records the detailed state within that phase. Lifecycle mappings translate legacy status values by table into the appropriate CSDM lifecycle stage/status pair. Lifecycle objects apply lifecycle definitions to CI types, which controls the available detailed status values."},{"n":226,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is tasked with moving various CMDB status attributes to life-cycle objects. The Administrator chooses to configure this by using the ‘reverse sync choice’ option. \\ \\ Which reverse sync choice attribute should the Administrator select?","choices":{"A":"If the attribute is set to ‘false’, then the legacy state value changes the life cycle value.","B":"If the attribute is set to ‘true’, then the life cycle value changes the legacy state value.","C":"If the attribute is set to ‘true’, then the legacy state value changes the life cycle value.","D":"If the attribute is set to ‘false’, then the life cycle value changes the legacy state value."},"answer":"B","exp":"A life-cycle mapping normally uses a legacy status value as the source to set the CSDM life-cycle value pair. Enabling reverse synchronization reverses that direction, so the life-cycle value updates the legacy state value.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow: Life cycle mapping form](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/common-service-data-model-csdm/csdm-life-cycle-mapping-form.html?contentId=pqCEWiVx6dheaSNluvD9~g) · [ServiceNow: Specify how to map legacy life-cycle states to CMDB states](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/washingtondc/servicenow-platform/common-service-data-model-csdm/create-life-cycle-migration.html)"},{"n":227,"domain":"Navigate","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator wants to create a CMDB 360 query in CMDB Workspace to determine whether reports can help manage CMDB data. \\ \\ Which items can CMDB 360 query? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Gaps in attribute data from different data sources","B":"Different attribute values from different data sources","C":"Duplicate CIs created from different data sources","D":"Unique CIs created from different data sources"},"answer":"AB","exp":"CMDB 360 supports Find Gap queries to analyze gaps in data reported by discovery sources and Compare Attribute Values queries to identify CI attributes whose values differ across discovery sources or from the CMDB.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CMDB 360 experience in a workspace](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb360-exp-cmdb-workspace.html) · [Create a Compare Attribute Values query](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/workspc-mltsrc-query-comp-attr-value.html)"},{"n":228,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"Over time, a company’s CMDB has built up several custom CI classes for similar device types (for example: `u_cmdb_ci_custom_router`, `u_cmdb_ci_special_switch`, etc.). This has caused data fragmentation, reporting inefficiencies, and integration challenges. \\ \\ How should the CMDB team resolve this issue? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Utilize CI Class Manager to consolidate custom classes into standard CMDB classes","B":"Keep all existing custom classes to avoid potential risks associated with data migration","C":"Delete all custom classes and manually recreate CIs under appropriate standard classes, ensuring proper classification","D":"Move CIs from custom classes to standard ServiceNow classes, mapping attributes correctly"},"answer":"AD","exp":"ServiceNow recommends rationalizing custom CMDB data by identifying the target CMDB classes, mapping attributes, and moving CIs from existing classes to the appropriate CMDB classes. CI Class Manager provides centralized management of the CMDB class hierarchy and class definitions, supporting class-model consolidation rather than preserving redundant custom classes. A controlled migration retains CIs and their related objects; deleting and manually recreating CIs risks losing data and relationships.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CI Class Manager](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/ci-class-manager-landing-page.html) · [Synchronize existing data](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/common-service-data-model-csdm/migrate.html)"},{"n":229,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is reviewing operational CI records that have no owners and are more than 1 year old. \\ \\ Which recommended Data Manager action should the CMDB Administrator take to retire these records?","choices":{"A":"Create a scheduled job","B":"Create a policy","C":"Create a business rule"},"answer":"B","exp":"CMDB Data Manager uses life-cycle policies to govern bulk CI operations. A Retire policy can target CIs with no owner that are older than one year and retire them according to the active retirement definition for their CI class.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [Working with CMDB Data Manager](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-data-management.html) · [Create a CMDB Data Manager policy](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/data-manager-create-policy-wrkspc.html)"},{"n":230,"domain":"Ingest","ctx":-1,"q":"An ACMDB Administrator wants to fully use the CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB feature. \\ \\ How does this feature help? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Automatically stores last record from each discovery source for view and assignment","B":"Allows the CMDB to recompute after a reconciliation rule change, without waiting for a new data load","C":"Allows defining reconciliation rules between discovery sources changing values","D":"Provides a comprehensive up-to-date assessment of the company’s CMDB quality"},"answer":"BC","exp":"CMDB 360 preserves raw data for each CI and discovery-source combination, including values not selected by reconciliation. Administrators can modify reconciliation rules and recompute CMDB data using those retained values without waiting for another data load. It also supports dynamic reconciliation rules that determine how values from multiple discovery sources are reconciled.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow CMDB 360 documentation](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/multisource-cmdb.html?contentId=kKiSmxGqbed33QEjCQGspw)"},{"n":231,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator is working in CMDB Workspace and has enabled Multisource CMDB. \\ \\ Which tab is now populated when Multisource CMDB is enabled?","choices":{"A":"Insights","B":"CMDB 360","C":"Home","D":"Management"},"answer":"B","exp":"Multisource CMDB functionality is provided through the CMDB 360 experience in CMDB Workspace. The CMDB 360 view displays and analyzes data from the discovery sources that report CI attribute values.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CMDB 360](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/multisource-cmdb.html) · [CMDB 360 view in CMDB Workspace](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/xanadu/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-workspace-cmdb360-view.html)"},{"n":232,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"As part of a CMDB improvement initiative, a team is assessing the effectiveness of the CMDB Data Foundations Dashboard. \\ \\ Which describes a key benefit of the dashboard?","choices":{"A":"Automates the resolution of all CMDB data issues","B":"Improves visibility into CMDB health and data quality","C":"Eliminates the need for CMDB audits"},"answer":"B","exp":"The CMDB Data Foundations Dashboard provides metrics and insights that help teams monitor CMDB health, validate data and configurations, and identify risks affecting data quality. It supports visibility and remediation planning rather than automatically resolving all issues or replacing audits.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CMDB Data Foundations dashboard](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-data-foundations-dashboard.html)"},{"n":233,"domain":"Navigate","ctx":-1,"q":"Within the CMDB Workspace Intelligent Search UI element, which option is an alternative to using Natural Language Query (NLQ)?","choices":{"A":"Go to Query Builder","B":"Use conditional search instead","C":"Assign important actions","D":"Create report"},"answer":"B","exp":"CMDB Workspace Intelligent Search offers conditional search as an alternative to NLQ. Conditional search uses a basic condition builder to define searches for configuration items of a particular class.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [Explore and Search view — ServiceNow documentation](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/sg-workspace-search-explore-view.html?contentId=8zivXUAqLG7POsU03KWCPA)"},{"n":234,"domain":"Navigate","ctx":-1,"q":"Which button is shown alongside the search results when a Natural Language Query (NLQ) that involves multiple tables is executed?","choices":{"A":"View Unified Map","B":"View Report","C":"View Data Manager Policy","D":"View in Query Builder"},"answer":"D","exp":"For an NLQ-generated CMDB query that contains more than one table, ServiceNow displays **View in Query Builder**. It opens the fully constructed query on the CMDB Query Builder canvas for further editing.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow: Intelligent Search for CMDB](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/intelligent-search-cmdb.html?contentId=Co0gv5d8ES8Tbh1I9g3ORQ)"},{"n":235,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager manages the CMDB for a large enterprise and must establish rules for moving CIs through life-cycle stages including operational, retired, archived, and deleted. \\ \\ Match each key life-cycle-management aspect to the activity needed to implement it.","choices":{},"answer":"","exp":"Archiving preserves inactive CIs without removing their historical record, while deletion removes obsolete records under retention rules. Certification policy validates CI attributes against required business values. Attestation is a scheduled review in which responsible users confirm or reject the CI information, maintaining CMDB accuracy.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow: Working with CMDB Data Manager](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-data-management.html) · [ServiceNow: CIs attestation](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/attesting-cis.html)"},{"n":236,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator notices that the **Hardware CIs Missing Serial Numbers** metric is trending upward in the CMDB Data Foundations Dashboard. Using the Get Well Playbook, the Administrator identifies the root cause and remediates the issue. \\ \\ The Administrator now wants to run a monthly report to monitor the number of Hardware CIs without a serial number. \\ \\ Which play would be used?","choices":{"A":"Data Governance","B":"Fix","C":"Analysis"},"answer":"A","exp":"Data Governance covers the ongoing oversight and periodic review of CMDB data-quality results after remediation. A monthly report that tracks Hardware CIs lacking serial numbers is therefore a governance monitoring activity, whereas Analysis determines the cause and Fix performs the remediation. ServiceNow defines the Hardware CIs Missing Serial Numbers tile as the count of CIs that are non-compliant because their serial number is empty.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CMDB Data Foundations dashboard](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-data-foundations-dashboard.html)"},{"n":237,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"An Asset Manager and a Configuration Manager must synchronize fields between CIs and Assets. \\ \\ How is this achieved in ServiceNow using the baseline system?","choices":{"A":"Scheduled jobs","B":"Business Rules","C":"Scripts Includes","D":"UI Actions"},"answer":"B","exp":"When an asset has a corresponding CI, ServiceNow keeps their records synchronized through two baseline Business Rules: one updates CI fields after asset changes, and the other updates asset fields after CI changes.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow: Asset and CI management](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-asset-management/hardware-asset-management/c_ManagingAssets.html)"},{"n":238,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"The Configuration Management team finds the CMDB 360 dashboard useful and wants to continue using it. \\ \\ What is displayed on the CMDB 360 Dashboard? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"CIs entered via API calls","B":"Number of discovery sources","C":"CIs not reported by discovery sources","D":"CIs entered manually"},"answer":"BC","exp":"The CMDB 360 dashboard includes a Discovery sources tile showing the total number of discovery sources, and it includes a card for CIs not reported by discovery sources. Its purpose is to analyze multisource discovery data and discovery-source coverage, not to classify CIs by manual versus API entry.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CMDB 360 experience in a workspace](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb360-exp-cmdb-workspace.html) · [CMDB 360 view in CMDB Workspace](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-workspace-cmdb360-view.html?contentId=6qlwFbsvvKrHpyRHz_9r6Q)"},{"n":239,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"A customer uses Asset Management and Configuration Management processes and wants the asset and CI life cycles to remain synchronized. The CMDB Administrator has updated the **Hardware Status** field on a CI. \\ \\ Which field is automatically synchronized on the related Asset record?","choices":{"A":"Asset tag","B":"Installed","C":"State","D":"Substate"},"answer":"C","exp":"ServiceNow synchronizes a hardware CI’s Hardware Status with the associated asset’s State through the Asset-CI hardware status mapping, maintaining consistent lifecycle reporting. The mappings can also account for substates, but the CI Hardware Status change maps to the asset State field.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow: Asset and CI management](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-asset-management/hardware-asset-management/c_ManagingAssets.html) · [ServiceNow: Map asset state and CI hardware status](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-asset-management/asset-management/t_CreateAssetandCIHardwareStatusMapping.html?contentId=dyjOuoeFKd63m6LKxXfyCg)"},{"n":240,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"An IT operations team is making a change to an application environment and must ensure that the change is routed to the appropriate group for processing. \\ \\ Which CSDM data should the team use?","choices":{"A":"The Service Subscription by User list for task assignments","B":"The Assignment Group attribute on the CI","C":"The Approval Group from the Business Service Offering","D":"The Service Offering attribute to determine impacted environments"},"answer":"B","exp":"For change and change-task routing, the CI Assignment Group attribute identifies the group to which the work should be directed. The approval group controls approvals, while service offerings and service subscriptions do not provide the change-task routing value.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow: Change Management considerations](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-service-management/change-management/itsm-change-use-case-trouble.html)"},{"n":241,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator needs to configure the CMDB Compliance scorecard and consequently creates several audits. \\ \\ Which audit type is permitted in the CMDB Health Dashboard?","choices":{"A":"Compliance","B":"Architecture Compliance","C":"Desired State"},"answer":"C","exp":"CMDB Health compliance scores are based on Desired State audits, which compare configuration items’ actual attributes and relationships with their defined desired state. ServiceNow documentation identifies Desired State audits as a source for CMDB Health audit scoring.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow CMDB Health domain separation](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-health-domain-separation.html) · [ServiceNow Desired State](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/c_DesiredState.html)"},{"n":242,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"Which CMDB Health Dashboard metric helps improve the use of CMDB Data Manager retirement policies?","choices":{"A":"Audit","B":"Recommended","C":"Staleness","D":"Orphan"},"answer":"C","exp":"The Staleness metric measures CIs that have not been updated within the effective duration set by their staleness rule. Those outdated CIs can be targeted by CMDB Data Manager retirement policies to maintain a current CMDB.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CMDB Health KPIs and metrics](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/r_CMDBHealthMetrics.html) · [Working with CMDB Data Manager](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-data-management.html)"},{"n":243,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"An Asset Manager at a software start-up follows the company’s Change Management process to relocate several software development resources from their existing location to a new location. \\ \\ To which CSDM domain do the resources managed through Change Management belong?","choices":{"A":"Build and Integration (Build)","B":"Service Delivery (Manage Technical Service)","C":"Design and Planning (Design)","D":"Foundation","E":"Service Consumption (Sell/Consume)"},"answer":"D","exp":"Locations are common referential data in CSDM and are stored in the Foundation domain. A relocation processed through Change Management updates that foundational location context; Change Management does not change the CSDM domain classification of the location data.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [Foundation domain in the CSDM model](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/common-service-data-model-csdm/foundation-domain.html)"},{"n":244,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"Where does the CMDB Administrator configure tasks for CIs identified as orphans?","choices":{"A":"System Properties","B":"Health Metrics","C":"CI Class Manager","D":"CMDB Health Dashboard"},"answer":"B","exp":"In CMDB Health preferences, the **Health Metrics** configuration for the Orphan metric includes the **Create Task** setting. Enabling it causes a task to be created when a CI fails the orphan health test.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [Configure KPI and metrics preferences](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/t_ConfigureCMDBHealthMetrics.html)"},{"n":245,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"A facilities department wants to use ServiceNow to store location data `[cmn_location]`, but is concerned that other data sources could create duplicate records. \\ \\ Why should facilities use the Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE)? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Prevents inserts from unwanted data sources","B":"Uses relationships to determine insert or update of CI records","C":"Uses unique identification to determine insert or update of CI records","D":"Prevents updates from unwanted data sources"},"answer":"CD","exp":"IRE uses identification rules or unique identifiers to determine whether incoming data matches an existing record, so it can update that record rather than create a duplicate. Reconciliation restricts record and attribute updates to authorized data sources, protecting data integrity when multiple sources contribute data. ServiceNow documents that IRE supports certain non-CMDB tables and centrally applies identification and reconciliation across data sources.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [Exploring CMDB Identification and Reconciliation](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/xanadu/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/exploring-ire-d72863e17266.html) · [Components and process of Identification and Reconciliation](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/c_CompsandProcessIDandReconcil.html)"},{"n":246,"domain":"Ingest","ctx":-1,"q":"Drag the ServiceNow product to the outcome by using the CMDB.","choices":{},"answer":"","exp":"Asset Management tracks configuration-item and asset lifecycle information. Event Management can create incidents from configured event thresholds. Incident Management relies on CMDB data to identify affected configuration items and speed resolution. Change Management uses CI relationships for downstream impact analysis when planning upgrades."},{"n":247,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"An organization must ensure that whenever a parent CI’s Life Cycle Stage changes, the Life Cycle Stage for its child CIs is automatically updated. \\ \\ What action should the organization take to accomplish this?","choices":{"A":"Create a new CI class for Life Cycle Stage management","B":"Use a Transform Map to update Life Cycle Stage statuses","C":"Use Data Manager to set up Life Cycle Stage automation"},"answer":"C","exp":"ServiceNow dependent CI management uses CMDB Data Manager to process life-cycle updates for dependent CIs affected by changes to a parent CI. Data Manager policies and dependent-CI processing provide the relationship-based automation needed for cascading CI life-cycle operations.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow: Dependent CIs management](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/manage-dependent-ci.html) · [ServiceNow: Working with CMDB Data Manager](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-data-management.html)"},{"n":248,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"A ServiceNow Process Owner wants to use Business Application records in ServiceNow to guide business decisions. \\ \\ How would the Process Owner use them?","choices":{"A":"Application rationalization","B":"Impacted applications for a Change Request","C":"Application availability"},"answer":"A","exp":"Application rationalization uses Business Application portfolio data and indicators to support strategic decisions such as whether to invest in, sustain, migrate, or retire an application.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [Rationalization of business applications](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/application-portfolio-management/eaw-rationalize-business-applications.html)"},{"n":249,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager must ensure that every device in the CMDB has a unique serial number to prevent the risk of duplicate CIs being created. \\ \\ Which management tool identifies CIs that lack serial numbers?","choices":{"A":"CSDM Data Foundations Dashboard","B":"CMDB Data Foundations Dashboard","C":"CMDB Data Manager","D":"CI Class Manager"},"answer":"B","exp":"The CMDB Data Foundations Dashboard monitors CMDB health metrics, including the Hardware CIs Missing Serial Numbers tile. This metric identifies applicable hardware CIs with an empty serial number so they can be investigated and remediated, helping preserve CI identification quality.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow: CMDB Data Foundations dashboard](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-data-foundations-dashboard.html)"},{"n":250,"domain":"Navigate","ctx":-1,"q":"A Service Owner has used the Unified Map filter panel to show particular CI types and layers. \\ \\ How can the Service Owner save the filter selections?","choices":{"A":"Save the filter options as a preset","B":"Reconfigure the filter options each time","C":"Create a favorite using the banner"},"answer":"A","exp":"Unified Map filter settings can be saved as a user preset and later applied to a map. This preserves selections such as CI classes and layer criteria for reuse.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow: Manage a user preset](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/unified-map/unified-map-manage-preset-filter.html?contentId=T_6rG8sI8KLHmmp7dr6iIw)"},{"n":251,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"A company must ensure that its IT assets meet security and regulatory requirements. It wants to track compliance details—such as GDPR or HIPAA—against its CMDB objects. \\ \\ Which approach can be used?","choices":{"A":"Associate compliance identifiers with CSDM objects","B":"Create custom compliance identifiers in the CMDB","C":"Use the Service Catalog to request compliance tracking for CSDM objects"},"answer":"A","exp":"Compliance identifiers can be associated with CSDM objects to record which security or regulatory obligations, such as GDPR or HIPAA, apply to each modeled asset or service. CSDM provides the CMDB-based data model and relationships used to organize these objects; CMDB identification rules instead uniquely identify CIs, and the Service Catalog does not provide the compliance-association mechanism.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CSDM data domains](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/common-service-data-model-csdm/csdm-conceptual-model.html) · [Identification rules](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/c_IdentificationRules.html)"},{"n":252,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"An ACMDB Administrator has been assigned to improve CMDB health and bring the organization’s CMDB into alignment with ServiceNow best practices. \\ \\ How does the CMDB Data Foundation Dashboard Playbook assist in this situation?","choices":{"A":"Replaces the CMDB Health Dashboard","B":"Integrates third party discovery tools automatically","C":"Uses a step-by-step approach to improving CMDB data quality"},"answer":"C","exp":"The CMDB Data Foundation Dashboard identifies CMDB data-quality and best-practice issues, and its playbook links provide remediation guidance. This supplies a step-by-step approach for correcting data-quality problems and tracking improvement.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CMDB and CSDM Data Foundations Dashboards Introduction](https://www.servicenow.com/community/cmdb-articles/cmdb-and-csdm-data-foundations-dashboards-introduction/ta-p/3290419)"},{"n":253,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"The CMDB Configuration Manager needs to ensure that every Windows Server has more than 4 GB of RAM. \\ \\ Which metric in the CMDB Health Dashboard is configured?","choices":{"A":"Orphan","B":"Recommended","C":"Audit"},"answer":"C","exp":"The Audit metric evaluates CMDB data for compliance with predefined audit certificates or templates. A rule requiring Windows Server CIs to have more than 4 GB of RAM is an attribute-value compliance check, so it is configured as an audit.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CMDB Health KPIs and metrics](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/r_CMDBHealthMetrics.html) · [Overview of CMDB Health](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/overview-cmdb-health.html)"},{"n":254,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator must display only principal CIs as selectable on a change management form. \\ \\ Which class is recommended to designate as a Principal Class in this scenario?","choices":{"A":"‘Disk’ Class","B":"‘Windows Server’ Class","C":"‘Network Adapter’ Class"},"answer":"B","exp":"Principal classes should represent business-critical, independently managed infrastructure CIs that have meaningful service impact and are in scope for operational processes such as change management. A Windows Server fits that role; a disk and a network adapter are dependent component CIs rather than principal service-impacting CIs.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [Update Principal Class filter](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/update-principal-class-filter.html) · [Key CMDB success advisor concepts](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-sa-key-concepts.html)"},{"n":255,"domain":"Ingest","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator uses import sets to populate non-discoverable CI data through the `CMDBTransformUtil()` script. \\ \\ Which transform-map attributes must be populated? (Choose two.)","choices":{"A":"Serial Number field","B":"Coalesce field","C":"Source field","D":"Target field"},"answer":"CD","exp":"CMDBTransformUtil uses CMDB Identification and Reconciliation to identify and update CIs, so transform-map field maps must define the incoming import-set attribute and the CMDB attribute it maps to: the Source field and Target field. Coalescing is not required for CI identification, and a serial number is required only when an applicable identification rule uses it.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CMDBTransformUtil - Global](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/api-reference/server-api-reference/c_CMDBTransformUtilAPI.html) · [Create a field map](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/integrate-applications/system-import-sets/t_CreatingAFieldMap.html)"},{"n":256,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"Which ServiceNow capability provides predefined integrations specifically built to simplify integration with external systems?","choices":{"A":"Service Mapping","B":"Service Graph Connectors","C":"Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE)","D":"Agent Client Collector (ACC)"},"answer":"B","exp":"Service Graph Connectors are predefined integrations that ingest third-party and API data into the CMDB, providing a simplified, standardized way to integrate external systems. Service Mapping, IRE, and ACC serve discovery/mapping, CMDB data-governance, and endpoint-collection functions rather than providing those predefined integrations.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [Getting started with Service Graph Connectors](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-sgc-intro.html)"},{"n":257,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator knows there are duplicate records in the CMDB and wants to understand the effect of running the **CMDB Health Dashboard Correctness Score Calculation** job. The following duplicate CIs exist in the CMDB: \\ \\ - Server A: Created on January 20, 2025 \\ - Server A: Created on January 21, 2025 \\ - Server A: Created on January 22, 2025 \\ \\ Which records will have their **Duplicate Of** field populated?","choices":{"A":"Server A: Created on January 20, 2025 and Created on January 22, 2025","B":"Server A: Created on January 21, 2025 and Created on January 22, 2025","C":"Server A: Created on January 20, 2025 and Created on January 21, 2025"},"answer":"B","exp":"For a duplicate CI set, one CI is the main CI and its `duplicate_of` field remains empty; every other CI has `duplicate_of` set to reference that main CI. The earliest-created Server A record, from January 20, 2025, remains the main CI, so the January 21 and January 22 records are populated as duplicates.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow: CMDB Health KPIs and metrics](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/r_CMDBHealthMetrics.html) · [ServiceNow: Duplicate CIs remediation](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/de-duplication-tasks.html)"},{"n":258,"domain":"Ingest","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager is importing data into the CMDB while preserving CMDB integrity. The Manager plans to use the Robust Transformation Engine (RTE). \\ \\ Why does the Configuration Manager use the RTE?","choices":{"A":"It searches the CMDB for already existing CIs and updates the CIs with the latest data sets.","B":"It imports data from an external data source and pushes it to the staging table.","C":"It takes in the definition for how data should be converted from an object to the IRE.","D":"It inserts records into the CMDB in the correct classes and avoids duplicate data."},"answer":"C","exp":"The Robust Transform Engine maps and transforms raw source data from staging tables according to an ETL definition and creates payloads for the Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE). IRE performs CI identification, reconciliation, class insertion, and duplicate prevention.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [IntegrationHub ETL](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/integration-hub-etl/integrationhub-etl.html?contentId=YWEzW4gBxOg2CQ9qzG60mQ) · [RTETransformer - Scoped](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/api-reference/server-api-reference/RTETransScopedAPI.html)"},{"n":259,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"A Configuration Manager observes that the CMDB Health Dashboard Completeness Key Performance Indicator (KPI) is low. \\ \\ What can the Configuration Manager do to obtain a KPI that represents only managed CIs?","choices":{"A":"Nothing, the health score is calculated for the whole CMDB","B":"Configure health inclusion rules for the relevant CI classes","C":"Create a business rule to filter the CMDB health results"},"answer":"B","exp":"CMDB Health inclusion rules filter the CIs included in health calculations and shown on the CMDB Health Dashboard. Configuring rules for the applicable CI classes limits Completeness evaluation to the managed CIs that meet those rules.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [Create health inclusion rule](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/create-health-inclusion-rule.html?contentId=RC3UPFdFos3RLVwryRAF_Q)"},{"n":260,"domain":"Ingest","ctx":-1,"q":"How is an Application Service created with relationships to its underlying infrastructure?","choices":{"A":"Agent Client Collector","B":"Event Management","C":"ServiceNow Discovery","D":"Service Mapping"},"answer":"D","exp":"Service Mapping discovers application services and builds maps of the devices, applications, configuration items, and relationships that support them. It therefore creates the application-service relationship view of underlying infrastructure.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [Service Mapping](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-operations-management/service-mapping/c_ServiceMappingOverview.html) · [Service instances (Application services)](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/application-services.html)"},{"n":261,"domain":"Navigate","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Administrator has built a complex CMDB query in ServiceNow with CMDB Query Builder. The query retrieves detailed information about business services, servers, and application services related to the 'Network Service! Another team is working on a similar project in a different ServiceNow instance and wants to use the complex query. \\ \\ Which approach should the other team use to transfer the complex query to the other instance?","choices":{"A":"Export the query using an Export XML, then use the Import XML option on the other instance","B":"Export the query as a Report and provide the other team with the exported file, and then import it as a new report in their instance","C":"Export the query using an Update Set, then import the update set in the other instance","D":"Export the query from within Query Builder, then the other team can use the import query to import it directly"},"answer":"D","exp":"CMDB Query Builder can export a saved CMDB query definition as an XML file from within Query Builder. The destination instance imports that file by using the **Import query** action in CMDB Query Builder, which makes the query available among its saved queries. Update-set transfer is an alternative maintained for backward compatibility.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow: Export and import a CMDB query](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/export-import-query.html)"},{"n":262,"domain":"Ingest","ctx":-1,"q":"The IRE has detected duplicates for a single CI. \\ \\ Which CI will the IRE update?","choices":{"A":"The oldest CI determined by the creation date.","B":"The newest CI determined by the creation date.","C":"The CI with the most recent updated date."},"answer":"A","exp":"When IRE detects duplicate CIs and processes them with duplicate skipping enabled, it selects and updates the oldest duplicate CI. That CI becomes the main CI, while the other records are marked as duplicates; age is determined by creation date.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow: Detecting duplicate CIs](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/id-detect-dup-ci.html?contentId=hFfrI_zlUnGeFaHBYwICEg)"},{"n":263,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"When viewing a CMDB record, a CMDB Administrator wants to determine whether it is a duplicate CI. \\ \\ Which field on the CI record identifies this?","choices":{"A":"The ‘Duplicate’ checkbox is checked.","B":"The ‘Discovery Status’ field has a value of ‘Duplicate’.","C":"The ‘Duplicate Of’ field is populated."},"answer":"C","exp":"ServiceNow marks duplicate CIs by populating the `duplicate_of` attribute (displayed as **Duplicate Of**) with a reference to the main CI. A populated value therefore identifies the CI as a duplicate.\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow — Duplicate CIs remediation](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/de-duplication-tasks.html)"},{"n":264,"domain":"Ingest","ctx":-1,"q":"A CMDB Manager is responsible for ensuring CI data accuracy throughout the organization and has identified opportunities to improve data quality by changing how conflicting values from multiple discovery sources are resolved. \\ \\ Which CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB capability directly supports the Manager’s ability to refine and validate these changes?","choices":{"A":"Automatically archives CIs that have not been updated by multiple sources within the same calendar quarter.","B":"Eliminates the need for identification rules by allowing all discovery sources to create CIs without matching criteria.","C":"Permanently locks CI records so that only the highest-priority discovery source can make updates.","D":"Allows reconciliation rules to be modified and CMDB data to be recomputed using the latest rules and the complete historical record contributed by each data source."},"answer":"D","exp":"CMDB 360 retains discovery-source details and proposed CI attribute values, including rejected updates. The Manager can modify reconciliation rules and recompute CI attribute values to apply those changes, while comparing source values to validate the results. ([servicenow.com](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/zurich/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/multisource-cmdb.html?contentId=PV3F7u84c1QYmqWH1ARqGg\\u0026utm_source=openai))\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CMDB 360/Multisource CMDB](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/zurich/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/multisource-cmdb.html) · [Recompute CI attribute values](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/recompute-attribute-values.html)"},{"n":265,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"A ServiceNow organization is setting up a governance structure for its CMDB implementation. The organization needs to assign accountability for ensuring that CI data meets organizational standards, resolving data inconsistencies, and maintaining ongoing data accuracy across discovery sources. \\ \\ Which role should be given these data-quality and governance responsibilities?","choices":{"A":"IT Asset Manager","B":"CMDB Process Owner","C":"CI Analyst","D":"CMDB Architect","E":"Service Owner"},"answer":"B","exp":"The CMDB Process Owner is the best available choice for overarching governance: the role establishes and improves configuration management processes, including data verification and audit processes. CI analysts and configuration managers support operational remediation, source coordination, and ongoing data maintenance under that governance framework. ([servicenow.com](https://www.servicenow.com/community/s/cgfwn76974/attachments/cgfwn76974/impact-events/40/1/2024.4.23%20ServiceNow%20Impact%20%2B%20ITOM.pdf?utm_source=openai))\\ \\ **Learn more:** [ServiceNow Impact: CMDB RACI and roles](https://www.servicenow.com/community/s/cgfwn76974/attachments/cgfwn76974/impact-events/40/1/2024.4.23%20ServiceNow%20Impact%20%2B%20ITOM.pdf) · [Data Management and Governance](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/impact/accelerator-and-initiative-list/data-mgt-governance.html)"},{"n":266,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"During a CMDB redesign project, a CMDB Administrator must document the authoritative data sources for each principal CI class and the attributes that trigger CI identification. \\ \\ Which CMDB management tool brings all this information together?","choices":{"A":"CMDB Data Foundations Dashboard","B":"CMDB Data Manager","C":"CI Class Manager","D":"CMDB Workspace"},"answer":"C","exp":"CI Class Manager provides a central place to view and manage class-level identification and reconciliation rules. Identification rules specify the attributes used to identify CIs, while reconciliation rules define which data sources are trusted to update CI attributes. ([servicenow.com](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/ci-class-manager-landing-page.html?utm_source=openai))\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CI Class Manager](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/ci-class-manager-landing-page.html) · [Create a CI identification rule](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/t_CreateCIIdentificationRule.html)"},{"n":267,"domain":"Configuration","ctx":-1,"q":"During a bulk import of user endpoint devices into the CMDB, Computer CI records are successfully populated with owner information in the Owned by [owned_by] field. The Asset Management team requires the same owner information to be automatically synchronized to the corresponding Asset records. \\ \\ Which automated approach should a Configuration Analyst implement?","choices":{"A":"Use the Asset-CI Field Mapping module to create a rule that replicates the Owned by value between the Computer CI and its associated Asset record.","B":"Use CI Class Manager to establish a parent-child relationship between the Computer and Asset classes.","C":"Configure a scheduled Transform Map or IntegrationHub ETL workflow to copy the Owned by value from Computer CIs to the Asset table.","D":"Implement a custom business rule on the Computer table to script the value into the related Asset record."},"answer":"A","exp":"Asset-CI Field Mapping supports automatic synchronization between fields on linked asset and CI records, including synchronization from a Computer CI to its associated asset. Owned by is already among the fields ServiceNow lists as synchronized, so the existing mapping and record links should be checked before creating a duplicate mapping. ([servicenow.com](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-asset-management/asset-management/t_CreateAssetandCIFieldsMapping.html?utm_source=openai))\\ \\ **Learn more:** [Map asset and CI fields](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-asset-management/asset-management/t_CreateAssetandCIFieldsMapping.html) · [Asset and CI management](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/zurich/it-asset-management/hardware-asset-management/c_ManagingAssets.html)"},{"n":268,"domain":"Govern","ctx":-1,"q":"A Windows administration team needs to organize Windows Server CIs for targeted Incident Management and Change Management workflows. \\ \\ Which approaches can the team use to create logical groupings within CMDB groups? (Choose two options.)","choices":{"A":"Manually select specific Windows Server instances and assign them to a named CMDB group.","B":"Use tag-based queries to automatically assign Windows Server CIs to a named CMDB group.","C":"Use encoded queries to dynamically filter and group Windows Server CIs based on specific attribute conditions.","D":"Use reconciliation rules to assign CIs to groups based on data-source priority."},"answer":"AC","exp":"A default CMDB group can include individually selected CIs or CIs returned by an encoded query. An encoded query can filter Windows Server CIs by class and attribute conditions, allowing the group to reflect matching records. ([servicenow.com](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-groups.html?utm_source=openai))\\ \\ **Learn more:** [CMDB groups](https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/configuration-management-database-cmdb/cmdb-groups.html)"}]} ;
